ibuting writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:59:50-07:00","id":987358,"title":"","content":"This election has turned into Bizarro America. My liberal friends are posting the most vile stuff about Clinton. My conservative friends are sitting the election out and joking about asteroids destroying earth.<br /> <br /> I am pretty much a low information voter this election because I don't have the time or energy to shovel though the bullshit. I don't want to vote third party because most of their policies are crazier than the main two (Vaccinate your kids, people!). I don't want to vote Trump because I know him from old. He had a lot of business dealing in my home town of West Palm Beach.<br /> <br /> I was okay with voting for Hillary Clinton, but the noise is starting to make me question my sanity. (Or maybe it's the 60 hours a week I have been working) I don't think she murdered someone... right? Has she really lied under oath? She really isn't going to start a war... I guess.<br /> <br /> I just don't know anymore. At this point I am thankful I am living in Texas and a Democratic vote is like pissing into the wind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:07:24-07:00","id":987361,"title":"","content":"I'm just pissed my vote means nothing here in Arizona.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:16:38-07:00","id":987373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987353#post987353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm wary of trusting any content out of a network suspected of being part of a network dedicated to spreading propaganda for the Russian government. Did BBC or Al Jazeera not have a good enough citation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't find a link for Al-Jazeera or BBC that wasn't the entire hearing on youtube. If you find that reason objectionable there's also: The state department just losing $6bn while she was the Secretary of State, Her personal ties through the Clinton Foundation to world leaders known to be funding IS, her talking about escalating the situation with China by surrounding them with a ring of missiles, the fact she doesn't know that &quot;C&quot; stands for classified, the state department she was head of pressuring haiti into keeping its minimum wage cut (the argument can be made it wasn't her directly, however, it was her state department at the time which is still her responsibility.),her involvement with the coup in Honduras<br /> <br /> And before this turns into a pile on, ugly, or the thread gets closed this will be my last post in it because thats exactly where this is headed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:30:48-07:00","id":987377,"title":"","content":"Yesterday I saw a CNN headline that read, &quot;I would rather have a candidate that likes women than a cheat.&quot; The sheer amount of disinformation and cognitive dissonance on display, not in simply American politics, but American society in all this is astounding. Any notion that societal rape apologism doesn't exist has been, or in my cynicism, should have been swept away after seeing the response of average citizens, some evangelical leaders,pundits,etc. And to address the opening statements of the OP, well I can't say if I do or don't agree with Trumps policies because I HAVE YET TO HEAR ONE. The man's stilted less than grade school level speech could still probably have stuttered out something resembling policy that even the &quot;basket of deplorables.&quot; could have recognized but he's not even gotten that far. At best I feel like Capt. Lionel Mandrake, listening in horror while Gen. Jack D. Ripper as proxy for a disturbing amount of the American public, talks to me about how Clinton is going to steal our vital fluids.<br /> <br /> Perhaps in some sense it would be understandable if I simply threw my arms up into the air and said in bitterness that people forgot that the old saying about how democracy gives you the government you deserve was a warning and bathe in self righteousness while things fell apart. I certainly see others doing that. But I can't. My daughter, currently eleven, lives in this country and I want her to have a future that doesn't look grim and disenfranchised.<br /> <br /> I am not keen on personal information but I will share a small tidbit relevant to this. When I came back here, I moved out to California because my mother was trying to fight Leukemia and while going through the light stages of her chemotherapy she couldn't work as much and it's expensive to live in California. So I moved in with my parents and I worked and I helped as much as I could. I got sorta lucky after I stopped working for a shady air conditioning company when I found a job with benefits and paid vacation time. Then the economic collapse happened. The company ushered each person in to have a one on one with the store manager(hint this is a tactic that Walmart and other places use to make someone feel vulnerable) and dictated to us that you could either take a severance that wouldn't even cover one month of rent or pretty much get no hours. I banked on the fact that so many people would leave that they'd have to work SOMEONE and it might as well be me because I needed that more certain paycheck now to help out my parents than the uncertainty of a job search in a depression.<br /> <br /> I worked and found any and every excuse I could to stay at work and do whatever, including kind of piteously cleaning the grouting between store tiles in store while people are stepping over you during work hours because management wanted the store to look so bloody spic and span for a visit. Things got worse for my mother and she was put in a medical coma in the very upscale hospital out in Newport Beach. My father couldn't handle things and so I took over keeping people calm, calling family members, arraigning the details of people flying in from all kinds of places to see my mother. I pleaded with my job for something, anything to work out being able to keep the roof over our head while having time to work on all this. What I got was a snide cold shoulder from them. Eventually due to complications from an infection in her lungs the question was put to me about what to do. I was luckier than most, since I was a small child, seven or eight and on. Me and my mother had long conversations about death, dying, life,etc and we talked a lot about how being tied to a machine isn't living and neither of us would want that. Funny thing is, that didn't make it any easier as I'm sitting there holding her hand while they remove the breathing tube and I watch my mother die just after my twenty eighth birthday.<br /> <br /> Fast forward to Seattle and bouncing around jobs trying to find something meaningful and sustaining in this economy. Instead I got stuff like working for a Verizon call center where despite a public policy of handling disconnects due to death, you &quot;mysteriously&quot; get coachings on those calls after you take them and subtly told to find a way to suggest they keep the deceased person's line of service for oh I dunno a tablet. Where I had a court order in my favour that would have put much needed money in my pockets each month is ignored by the company, where they change my W4 status illegally and there's nothing I can do because I'm too poor to do anything about it. Where I put in my two weeks notice and the company asks me to make a written two weeks notice statement, which I do then I find out from unemployment that the company tells them I didn't give notice so I get nothing.<br /> <br /> So I guess the question is why I am sharing this now long winded bit of personal information. To try to bring this point across to you. Do you know how you sound when you bring out stuff like that you support the &quot;policies&quot; of a man who brags about how rich he is to sexually assault someone. Who talks about Soros being some sort of super villain, that you despise socialism yet I wonder if you really understand the terminology. Some of us out there, well actually A LOT of us, are suffering tangibly. Our capacity to feed and clothe ourselves, yet alone the notion of ever getting the opportunity to do something to more permanently(in a sense), better our situations. As a veteran, as a citizen, as a son of a woman who deserved better. I am so so so sick of hearing conspiracy theories when we need theories of governance, rants about political purity when we need smart political pragmatism that stares the problems facing the U.S. and the world in the face and seeks to solve them. Clinton isn't perfect, sure I would have like Sanders. But I understand how the political process works and I'll vote for Clinton. Not just because the alternative is a raging dumpster fire. But because I'd like to at least have a chance at my kid having something resembling a future.<br /> <br /> /rantdone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-15-2016, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:48:29-07:00","id":987385,"title":"","content":"If you absolutely can't bring yourself to vote for Trump or Clinton, you should vote for Gary Johnson. He isn't going to win anyway, so his individual faults aren't an issue. You don't vote for him because he'll win, you vote for him to express you dissatisfaction with Trump and Clinton and to give a third party more potential influence in the future - which could eventually lead to greater accountability for the Republican and Democrat Parties. If you have the chance to send that sort of message with your vote, why would you refuse to vote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:03:27-07:00","id":987393,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Sergeant Brother. I'm sure there's many presidents who, coming into office, weren't aware of the specifics for certain world issues others think they should be. Johnson doesn't have the power of the Democratic or Republican party behind them to help them get past it.<br /> <br /> If you think he's an idiot for other reasons, at least write in a candidate you believe in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:11:14-07:00","id":987397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987385#post987385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you absolutely can't bring yourself to vote for Trump or Clinton, you should vote for Gary Johnson. He isn't going to win anyway, so his individual faults aren't an issue. You don't vote for him because he'll win, you vote for him to express you dissatisfaction with Trump and Clinton and to give a third party more potential influence in the future - which could eventually lead to greater accountability for the Republican and Democrat Parties. If you have the chance to send that sort of message with your vote, why would you refuse to vote?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, I'd agree in theory but not in practice. Our Presidential system is so loaded that it's going to be nearly impossible to change in the short term. That said, this election looks like it's going to be a blow-out. So vote the candidate that best represents your intents, particularly if you weren't planning on voting at all. I normally vote Green Party, but I'll be voting Clinton this year. I find her fairly repulsive, but I couldn't live with myself if I voted against her and Trump one.<br /> <br /> Mostly get out there because if we're ever going to enact change, it's going to happen downticket. Carefully research your congressional candidates and local representatives, stump for the people who represent you, and get your vote out there. Bottom-up is the way we change the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:24:36-07:00","id":987403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a vote for Gary Johnson just amounts to a vote that isn't contributing to keeping the power to fill Supreme Court Justice seats out of the hands of Donald Trump. Literally anyone would be better than him, I would vote for Sarah freaking Palin over him if she was running and I thought she had a chance of beating him. I'm sorry, but this is not the year to make a statement with your vote. The possibility of that man becoming Commander in Chief is too real and too dangerous not to do anything in my power to help avoid. And since Colorado is a swing state I have even more responsibility to help weight it away from swinging in his direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-14-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:31:14-07:00","id":987407,"title":"","content":"I would agree that this is a very important election and I'm personally not going to vote to make a statement, which is why I am voting for Donald Trump. But for those people, like the OP, who absolutely won't vote for Trump or Clinton, I think that it is better to use their vote to make a statement rather than not vote at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:31:52-07:00","id":987408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987403#post987403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a vote for Gary Johnson just amounts to a vote that isn't contributing to keeping the power to fill Supreme Court Justice seats out of the hands of Donald Trump. Literally anyone would be better than him, I would vote for George W. Bush over him if he was somehow able to run again and I thought he had a chance of winning, and I was vehemently anti-Bush. I'm sorry, but this is not the year to make a statement with your vote. The possibility of that man becoming Commander in Chief is too real and too dangerous not to do anything in my power to help avoid. And since Colorado is a swing state I have even more responsibility to help weight it away from swinging in his direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is the main reason why Clinton still gets my push of the button.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:37:40-07:00","id":987412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987407#post987407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would agree that this is a very important election and I'm personally not going to vote to make a statement, which is why I am voting for Donald Trump.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987407#post987407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for those people, like the OP, who absolutely won't vote for Trump or Clinton, I think that it is better to use their vote to make a statement rather than not vote at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There will functionally be no difference between voting for a third party and not voting. The system is fucked up like that, but this year is too important not to play the system's game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:50:02-07:00","id":987418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987158#post987158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're sounding a little bit Alex Jones-y with the whole &quot;evil globalists control the media&quot; bit there, buddy. But anyone who can see how wretched Trump is is a friend of mine. Clinton's no saint, but until the right can sever ties with the folks who hate the LGBTQ community I can't begon to consider any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you deny that there is a MASSIVE bias from the media towards the left, with the exception of fox news (and even they are starting to go left in some manners..)??<br /> <br /> Heck, the 19th debate, will be the first time a FOX news reporter has even Moderated a debate.. To me that just goes to show how one sided they seem to be..<br /> <br /> And as to the LGBTQRS hating.. Trump has several times, said he is not against them, but neither is a full on supporter of them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987163#post987163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not a big fan of Hillary, but she's better than Trump in my opinion, and she's the only candidate that has any chance of beating him. The two party system has put us between a rock and a hard place, just like it always does, but when the rock is as unappealing as Trump as a presidential candidate, a hard place looks pretty inviting by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>So someone who has had scandal, after scandal, some of which have cost US lives is better than someone who just keeps putting his foot in his mouth?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987403#post987403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a vote for Gary Johnson just amounts to a vote that isn't contributing to keeping the power to fill Supreme Court Justice seats out of the hands of Donald Trump. Literally anyone would be better than him, I would vote for Sarah freaking Palin</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't it the left that savaged the hell out of palin when she DID run as VP under Mccain back in 08.? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:56:04-07:00","id":987422,"title":"","content":"Trumps tepid lack of hatred for LGBT people certainly makes me feel so so so much better about his rampant sexism, bragging about sexual assault, his hatred of the concept of freedom of and from religion as it's directed towards Muslims(and now Jews apparently), his authoritarian intentions in regards to the use of the U.S. military and the Attorney General, and his racism. Just to name a few things. And Palin should be happy right? I mean there are tensions with Russia currently and she can see them from her place in Alaska right. Also the idea that the Democrats are &quot;the left&quot; or that mainstream media sources are &quot;the left&quot; hah!<br /> <br /> Whenever I see these sort of attempts at excusing Trumps nature I just think of the scorpion and the frog but I don't think his supporters realize THEY are the frog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-14-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:05:42-07:00","id":987429,"title":"","content":"I dislike Hillary, not only for the things she has done but also because I find the idea of electing another Clinton into office to be a terrible mistake. I think one of the problems with America is that so much of the political power is controlled by a small group of elites, and electing Hillary will only make that problem worse.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I simply cannot bring myself to vote for Trump. When he first started his campaign I contemplated voting for him as a way to oppose the political status quo, but as the campaign has gone on I've realized that seeing him become president would simply be the worst possible outcome of all.<br /> <br /> If the Republicans had chosen any other candidate I would be casting a vote for them. But I simply can't bring myself to do it for Trump - worse, I can't bring myself to make a protest vote for a 3rd party candidate because I realize that could lead to Trump winning. Every other election I've voted, I've voted for a 3rd party presidential candidate, but I don't feel I can do that this year in good conscience. I feel like I have no choice but to hold my nose and vote Hillary because to do otherwise risks seeing Trump become president.<br /> <br /> In fact, I am almost considering voting a straight ticket for Democrats simply as a way of showing my absolute disgust for the Republican Party for being so willing to embrace someone like Trump.<br /> <br /> Honestly I am just profoundly saddened and disappointed by this election and still find it rather hard to believe that the Republicans decided to embrace the <i>one</i> person more odious than Hillary Clinton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:05:46-07:00","id":987430,"title":"","content":"Most leftists would say that MSNBC and other media outlets are not very liberal at all, which actually is fairly accurate.<br /> <br /> They are certainly left of the far right though, for diminishing values of what constitutes the left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:15:18-07:00","id":987436,"title":"","content":"Anyone who knows about the Southern Strategy, Barry Goldwater, and the last fourty years of Republican political opportunism shouldn't be terribly surprised at this election. This was a long time in the making but you can't spend decades cultivating an often impoverished, racist, high on conspiracy low on information demographic and then be surprised when this happens. There are real issues of economic inequality that the Democratic party, regardless of who is president, needs to address and have in many ways failed to address. But solutions will not be found in a party in full upheaval who has spent the majority of it's modern existence working to deny minorities of all sorts rights, continually pushed agendas that disproportionately benefits the rich and more importantly benefits the rich TO THE DETRIMENT of the vast majority of other Americans, encourages libertarian neo-feudalism and deregulation, courts the worst dregs of the religious right(and this election has shown those people really DO NOT care about morality, not even their own twisted sense of it) and whose starve the beast mentality has turned one branch of government into a paralyzed invalid and seeks to block the potential saving of another branch while locking themselves out of the third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","