/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987418#post987418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it the left that savaged the hell out of palin when she DID run as VP under Mccain back in 08.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. She is a terrible politician who pretty much ruined McCain's chances at the presidency. I used her as an example to emphasize how I would rather vote for <i>anyone</i> than Trump. Before the edit I originally used George W. Bush as the example but I changed it because that didn't make sense because he obviously can't run again. I am pretty Left, and I would rather the furthest Right of polititians be in charge than Donald Trump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:00:16-07:00","id":987480,"title":"","content":"I've voted Democrat ever since I was able to vote, not because I necessarily agree with everything on the Dem ticket, but because the Republican ticket courts interests that would literally murder me if they were aware of me and they thought they could get away with it.<br /> <br /> It turns out that I am a single issue voter and that issue is &quot;The continued safety of myself and others like me&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:07:45-07:00","id":987484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987440#post987440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, you can't not hate the queer community and then choose the man who signed one of the most LGBT-discriminatory bills into law as your running mate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think Trump's malignant narcissism really permits him to <i>hate</i> anyone; he probably just views everybody who is not Donald Trump with a kind of wanton and contemptuous neglect, like they're not really people at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11105-seviphas","name":"Seviphas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:50:00-07:00","id":987492,"title":"","content":"That's like saying he's not racist/sexist/whatever form of bigot you care to name, because he hates everyone equally. It's not actually an improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:26:36-07:00","id":987503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987480#post987480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've voted Democrat ever since I was able to vote, not because I necessarily agree with everything on the Dem ticket, but because the Republican ticket courts interests that would literally murder me if they were aware of me and they thought they could get away with it.<br /> <br /> It turns out that I am a single issue voter and that issue is &quot;The continued safety of myself and others like me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you are only confused and not being disingenuous. Unless you are the resurrected Osama Bin Laden or someone else trying to destroy this country, ie George Soros and company, no one wants you dead. I am a Republican, and I am sick and tired of being labeled a bigot and a racist because of it. I am a straight white christian male, so freakin what!? As a Catholic, a religious group along with Jews and Blacks targeted by the Democrat's militant group the KKK, I am offended by the implication. The KKK of Indiana in the 1920's listed the three groups they hated from greatest to least: Catholics, Jews, and Blacks. The three men I admire most, after Christ of course, is MLK, Booker T Washington, and Abraham Lincoln. What do they all have in common? Here is a hint, it rhymes with Depublican and they furthered the cause for civil liberties. Morgan Freeman said that racism will not end until we stop talking about race. I couldn't agree more.<br /> <br /> I may not condone the gay life style, but I do not care what people do or who they love. Hate the sin, not the sinner and all that jazz. I have supported gay marriage since the 90's. Marriage is a secular institution in America, so this is an easy vote for me. I am pro-life but I do not support the death penalty, because killing is killing. I treat everyone the same, with respect regardless if we agree or not. I refuse to tolerate the intolerant or those that wish harm to me, my family, or my country. Am I alone with this? We may not agree on many of these issues, but I hope we can all agree that we should respect each others opinions. So many people have equated the Republican party with racism, when that shoe belongs to the Democratic party, the party of slavery, Jim Crow and segregation, the KKK and MUCH more. If anyone thinks times have changed, they didn't pay attention when DNC staffers referred to Latino voters as &quot;Taco Bowls&quot;, or when HRC called Black youth &quot;Super Predators&quot; in 1996. HRC staffers referred to Sanders supporters as basement dwellers and plotted to use his Jewish faith against him in the primaries! They are talking about their own voter base here people!!! I am not saying that Democratic voters are this way, I am saying the DNC is. I am saying the Democratic politicians are this way. Just because one political party does some bad stuff, doesn't mean their voter base condones it. George W. Bush did some crappy stuff, doesn't mean I am cool with it just because I vote Republican, the same can be said for Democrats. HRC and the Clinton foundation sold American policy to the highest bidder, that doesn't mean her voters support political corruption. We all know that we never get the best possible candidate to vote for, we can only hope that we can live with giving them our vote. A growing number of Republican leaders and their voter base oppose Trump. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias","name":"Tobias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1090_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:48:21-07:00","id":987512,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1090-tobias\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1090_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1090\" data-vbnamecard=\"1090\">Tobias</a> You'll have a point when whites are targeted by the authorities in massively greater numbers than other races, or when anyone tries to campaign of keeping a registry of all those dangerous Christians and passes laws aimed at restricting the freedoms of cisgender and straight individuals. Until <i>any</i> of that happens, it remains that the bulk of Americas political right seems to be diametrically opposed to progressivism and for those of us who are literally in physical danger because of our ethnic/sexual/gender/religious identities it's fucking absurd to even consider the Republicans a valid political option.<br /> <br /> It's telling that a not-insignificant part of the Republican politicians only disavowed Trump after his comments regarding women, but said nothing when he proposed a ban on Muslims entering the country, called Mexicans rapists, or took on bigot extraordinaire Pence as his running mate. Any one of those things should've been just as damning as the shit that's come out in the last week, and the message that pulling support from him now presents is &quot;he can say all that shit, but he can't do anything affects white women, our daughters and wives.&quot; Fuck that.<br /> <br /> And I sure as hell don't appreciate you calling &quot;the gay lifestyle&quot; a sin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 10-14-2016, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:50:54-07:00","id":987514,"title":"","content":"Lincoln's Republican party is more like modern Democrats than the Republicans of today, though. Both sides have switched policies over the almost two centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":