se to tolerate the intolerant or those that wish harm to me, my family, or my country. Am I alone with this? We may not agree on many of these issues, but I hope we can all agree that we should respect each others opinions. So many people have equated the Republican party with racism, when that shoe belongs to the Democratic party, the party of slavery, Jim Crow and segregation, the KKK and MUCH more. If anyone thinks times have changed, they didn't pay attention when DNC staffers referred to Latino voters as &quot;Taco Bowls&quot;, or when HRC called Black youth &quot;Super Predators&quot; in 1996. HRC staffers referred to Sanders supporters as basement dwellers and plotted to use his Jewish faith against him in the primaries! They are talking about their own voter base here people!!! I am not saying that Democratic voters are this way, I am saying the DNC is. I am saying the Democratic politicians are this way. Just because one political party does some bad stuff, doesn't mean their voter base condones it. George W. Bush did some crappy stuff, doesn't mean I am cool with it just because I vote Republican, the same can be said for Democrats. HRC and the Clinton foundation sold American policy to the highest bidder, that doesn't mean her voters support political corruption. We all know that we never get the best possible candidate to vote for, we can only hope that we can live with giving them our vote. A growing number of Republican leaders and their voter base oppose Trump. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well my uncle tried to beat the gay out of me when I was sixteen. There's plenty of hate groups who want me dead in the abstract.<br /> <br /> But how gracious, how<i> magnanimous</i> of you to not hate me, just a large aspect of my personality that people have tried to kill me and people like me for since this country was founded and before. How christian of you to stop at refusing to condone me as a person and not move on to breaking my bones with a baseball bat.<br /> <br /> I'm honored.<br /> <br /> I'll break it down slowly and simply so maybe you can <i>fucking</i> understand my position instead of deciding that I'm attacking you personally.<br /> <br /> The Republican party decided to court aspects of the american people that they felt would help them get votes. Some of these aspects included vocal bigots. The republicans could, for a long while, continue to court them by winking and telling them that they agreed with their beliefs. These beliefs include &quot;Homosexuals are evil and should be killed&quot;<br /> <br /> Kindly <i>fuck right off.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:37:29-07:00","id":987531,"title":"","content":"I'm not DONE!<br /> <br /> It's also entirely disingenuous to claim that the Republican/Democratic parties of today are the same as the parties of the Civil War/Reconstruction eras.<br /> <br /> The fact is, Republicans have made their bed by courting these toxic aspects of America focused on hate. Donald's success was in large part because he didn't just court them like the mainstream Republican party, he got out a big fucking bullhorn and invited them over for a political orgy and they flocked to him because FINALLY there was someone who was serious about championing their causes. The rest of the party was forced to smile, nod and swallow their pride because they didn't want to alienate their base, but this last week or so has made that position entirely untenable for many of them them to keep supporting Donald. Every anti-republican ad in my area is basically &quot;this guy supported donald, and look what an appalling person he turned out to be. can you trust him?&quot; over clips of donald being the anus-faced darling of America\u2019s rotten heart that he constantly manages to be.<br /> <br /> The fact is that between Hillary and this scrotum full of Tang, this grotesque homunculus assembled from every spare dribble of semen ever fallen from the cheeto-stained fingers of a full-time Twitter troll, this hashmouthed nobody, this human-shaped bus full of date rapists, this whining squirming ham baby, this horror movie, this cancerous vivisection of the American Dream, this unmoderated internet comment section made flesh, this money pit, this jackoff fascist fuck Republicans have enshrined as the ideal person to represent our country, <i>I would still vote for Hillary even I disagreed with every aspect of her policy.</i><br /> <br /> Because lets be real, Hillary is the most qualified person in the entire history of the country to be POTUS.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I wouldn't shit in Donald's mouth to save him from starvation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:13:08-07:00","id":987544,"title":"","content":"A few things:<br /> <br /> 1) The old Republicans were not anti-bigotry, because nobody back then was. Lincoln might have been incredibly progressive for his time, but he was still racist as hell by modern standards.<br /> <br /> 2) The reason why the modern Republican party gets painted with the &quot;bigot&quot; brush is painfully simple: The Civil Rights Act. When JFK died and LBJ decided to push the civil rights policies JFK wanted to get done, he had a giant problem. We call them the Dixicrats. Those would be all those racist assholes that used to dominate the Democratic party. LBJ did what we want our political leaders to do. He did the right thing for the country, and ripped his party in half by telling the Dixicrats to go fuck themselves (and really that's not far off from what he actually said a few times... the recordings of LBJ being a crass jerk are amazing) if they weren't going to fall in line. And the Republicans welcomed the Dixicrats with open arms to create the Southern Strategy.<br /> <br /> So it's simple. The Democrats decided to tell the racists in their party to shut up and get on board with not being the party of racists any more, and the Republicans said, &quot;We'll take you if they don't want you anymore.&quot; And since then the Republican party hasn't been able to shed the stink of that act, because they willing got in bed with racists that the Democrats got rid of, and have yet to show the courage to rid themselves of the same groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:26:11-07:00","id":987549,"title":"","content":"Also, this is one of the insidious things about the Russians hacking the Democrats to reveal campaign strategy discussions:<br /> <br /> Yeah, lots of ugly shit was said in those discussions, because that's the job of campaign staff. They dig up everything they can. They find out what their candidate's weaknesses are. They find out what skeletons are in their opponent's closets. They come up with attack lines from high brow policy wonkery to low brow nonsense.<br /> <br /> And everyone gets outraged there because of how sick some of that stuff is (even though we've been doing it the whole freaking time we've been a country), but then forget that the campaign doesn't stop there. They forget that if a staffer mentioned X, but the campaign never uses X? It means the campaign decided X was a stupid thing to say. Someone suggested that there might be something with Bernie downplaying his Jewish faith and heritage, and someone more powerful said that's idiotic and it wasn't something that was used in the primaries.<br /> <br /> That's why campaigns keep this shit secret. Opposition research is a nasty business, that the public doesn't really want to know about, but everyone needs to do in modern elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:27:22-07:00","id":987552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987503#post987503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The three men I admire most, after Christ of course, is MLK, Booker T Washington, and Abraham Lincoln. What do they all have in common? Here is a hint, it rhymes with Depublican and they furthered the cause for civil liberties.</div> </div> </div> </div>That first one's not as true as you think and the other two are frankly irrelevant to the modern GOP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.politifact.com/virginia/statements/2016/jan/25/philip-van-cleave/van-cleave-wongly-says-martin-luther-king-jr-was-r/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://politifact.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/March_On_Washington_Photo_G5b15d_1.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politifact.com/virginia/statements/2016/jan/25/philip-van-cleave/van-cleave-wongly-says-martin-luther-king-jr-was-r/\" target=\"_blank\"> No, Martin Luther King Jr. was not a Republican </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.politifact.com/virginia/statements/2016/jan/25/philip-van-cleave/van-cleave-wongly-says-martin-luther-king-jr-was-r/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.politifact.com/virginia/statements/2016/jan/25/philip-van-cleave/van-cleave-wongly-says-martin-luther-king-jr-was-r/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Martin Luther King Jr. \"was a Republican.\" </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is absolutely true that the Democratic Parties of 1860-1920 were White Supremacists, just as it is absolutely true that they all abandoned the party in the 1960s as a result of the Civil Rights Act and Voter Registration Act. The Republicans welcomed them with open arms and are now facing the reality that LBJ knew was coming: If you welcome racists into your party, sooner or later they're going to be the loudest and largest block in your party because they'll drive everyone else away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:02:51-07:00","id":987609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987385#post987385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you absolutely can't bring yourself to vote for Trump or Clinton, you should vote for Gary Johnson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am all about protest voting, but as I despise the policies and actions of pretty much EVERY candidate (even the Green Party and Libertarians. HOW DOES THAT EVEN HAPPEN?) I'm going with Mickey Mouse.<br /> <br /> Goofus D. Dawg as VP.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/cor