man all along!!!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:27:12-07:00","id":987850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987833#post987833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep hoping it's one big performance art piece to try and see at what point Americans will see someone as too vile to support.<br /> <br /> Here's hoping that reveal is soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember Joe Rogan had a bit about how the only logical explanation for G. W. Bush winning <i>twice</i> is that the US government must be controlled by a think tank and the only way they coud be sure they had total control was to put a dumb guy in office. And the bit concluded with him saying &quot;and you know there's that one guy in the back of the room saying '...I think we could go dumber.&quot;<br /> <br /> He called it. In 2004, he called it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-15-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:59:56-07:00","id":987869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987429#post987429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Republicans had chosen any other candidate I would be casting a vote for them. But I simply can't bring myself to do it for Trump - worse, I can't bring myself to make a protest vote for a 3rd party candidate because I realize that could lead to Trump winning. Every other election I've voted, I've voted for a 3rd party presidential candidate, but I don't feel I can do that this year in good conscience. I feel like I have no choice but to hold my nose and vote Hillary because to do otherwise risks seeing Trump become president.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was us the people, not the republicans who picked him.. Heck the party on several times, looked like they were going to DENY him the nod, till they started seeing the backlash from voters...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987472#post987472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting his foot in his mouth is not the issue. Being an unabashed bigot, con man, and probable pedophile and rapist with no prior political experience and a terrible track record in the business world to boot is.</div> </div> </div> </div>And other than some accusations that seem to have crawled out of the woodwork, so damn close to the actual election, by the time they could be defended against, it will be to late to matter.. What proof do you have in that assessment that Trump is a rapist/pedo? And compare THAT to the fact hillary Defended her hubby against HIS RAPIST accusers, and it makes me wonder why you would support HER over Don??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987503#post987503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many people have equated the Republican party with racism, when that shoe belongs to the Democratic party, the party of slavery, Jim Crow and segregation, the KKK and MUCH more.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why i have never understood why so many blacks ARE life long democrats.. unless its cause of all the free stuff, or the schools are NOT teaching any of that in history classes..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987531#post987531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not DONE!<br /> <br /> It's also entirely disingenuous to claim that the Republican/Democratic parties of today are the same as the parties of the Civil War/Reconstruction eras.<br /> <br /> The fact is, Republicans have made their bed by courting these toxic aspects of America focused on hate. Donald's success was in large part because he didn't just court them like the mainstream Republican party, he got out a big fucking bullhorn and invited them over for a political orgy and they flocked to him because FINALLY there was someone who was serious about championing their causes. The rest of the party was forced to smile, nod and swallow their pride because they didn't want to alienate their base, but this last week or so has made that position entirely untenable for many of them them to keep supporting Donald. Every anti-republican ad in my area is basically &quot;this guy supported donald, and look what an appalling person he turned out to be. can you trust him?&quot; over clips of donald being the anus-faced darling of America\u2019s rotten heart that he constantly manages to be.<br /> <br /> The fact is that between Hillary and this scrotum full of Tang, this grotesque homunculus assembled from every spare dribble of semen ever fallen from the cheeto-stained fingers of a full-time Twitter troll, this hashmouthed nobody, this human-shaped bus full of date rapists, this whining squirming ham baby, this horror movie, this cancerous vivisection of the American Dream, this unmoderated internet comment section made flesh, this money pit, this jackoff fascist fuck Republicans have enshrined as the ideal person to represent our country, <i>I would still vote for Hillary even I disagreed with every aspect of her policy.</i><br /> <br /> Because lets be real, Hillary is the most qualified person in the entire history of the country to be POTUS.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I wouldn't shit in Donald's mouth to save him from starvation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pot, Meet Kettle.. You claim trump called over the haters.. BUT i have not heard a single trump supporter spew anywhere near the level of hatred and venom towards someone else as i just read... PERIOD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987656#post987656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congrats, you have silenced the opposition again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to be the left's favored tactic imo..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987713#post987713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She is as politician doing politician stuff. If she didnt cheat to reach office, then she would clearly didnt want it bad enough and the why would you vote someone who didnt put effort?</div> </div> </div> </div>So we should start rewarding cheating, lying and corruption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:06:19-07:00","id":987872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why i have never understood why so many blacks ARE life long democrats.. unless its cause of all the free stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the most offensive things I've read in weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:10:03-07:00","id":987875,"title":"","content":"As has been noted previously, the reason minorities tend to go Democrat is because they understand that the party stances have switched. Many have experienced the 'southern strategy' also mentioned above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:18:01-07:00","id":987879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987872#post987872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of the most offensive things I've read in weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whaaaat? You think black people are intelligent pragmatists rather than children just digging their grubby hands to the bottom of cereal box for the prize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:21:26-07:00","id":987881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987875#post987875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been noted previously, the reason minorities tend to go Democrat is because they understand that the party stances have switched. Many have experienced the 'southern strategy' also mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When you're an underrepresented minority, you have to be conservative in your vote. That was the mistake Bernie Sanders made. Regardless of Clinton's pragmatism, and the compromised policy her family represents (hello &quot;super-predators&quot; and toxic tax reforms), she represents slow and steady progress. Disadvantaged people don't engage in revolution unless that revolution makes pointed and earnest attempts to court them, because if a drastic change goes badly, the disenfranchised are going to get the worst of the backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:33:03-07:00","id":987891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And other than some accusations that seem to have crawled out of the woodwork, so damn close to the actual election, by the time they could be defended against, it will be to late to matter.. What proof do you have in that assessment that Trump is a rapist/pedo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no proof, but it doesn't matter. Even if he's innocent that doesn't absolve him of being a racist, sexist, misogynist, homophobic, transphobic bigot, nor does it change the fact that he has no prior political experience and doesn't seem to understand that the President is not the CEO of America, nor does it change the fact that he has driven multiple companies into bankruptcy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And compare THAT to the fact hillary Defended her hubby against HIS RAPIST accusers, and it makes me wonder why you would support HER over Don??</div> </div> </div> </div>What <i>her husband</i> has or hasn't done has <i>nothing</i> to do with <i>her</i> qualifications. Hillary Clinton is not Bill Clinton, shockingly enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-15-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:36:51-07:00","id":987893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tobias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987503#post987503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope you are only confused and not being disingenuous. Unless you are the resurrected Osama Bin Laden or someone else trying to destroy this country, ie George Soros and company, no one wants you dead. I am a Republican, and I am sick and tired of being labeled a bigot and a racist because of it. I am a straight white christian male, so freakin what!? As a Catholic, a religious group along with Jews and Blacks targeted by the Democrat's militant group the KKK, I am offended by the implication. The KKK of Indiana in the 1920's listed the three groups they hated from greatest to least: Catholics, Jews, and Blacks. The three men I admire most, after Christ of course, is MLK, Booker T Washington, and Abraham Lincoln. What do they all have in common? Here is a hint, it rhymes with Depublican and they furthered the cause for civil liberties. Morgan Freeman said that racism will not end until we stop talking about race. I couldn't agree more.<br /> <br /> I may not condone the gay life style, but I do not care what people do or who they love. Hate the sin, not the sinner and all that jazz. I have supported gay marriage since the 90's. Marriage is a secular institution in America, so this is an easy vote for me. I am pro-life but I do not support the death penalty, because killing is killing. I treat everyone the same, with respect regardless if we agree or not. I refuse to tolerate the intolerant or those that wish harm to me, my family, or my country. Am I alone with this? We may not agree on many of these issues, but I hope we can all agree that we should respect each others opinions. So many people have equated the Republican party with racism, when that shoe belongs to the Democratic party, the party of slavery, Jim Crow and segregation, the KKK and MUCH more. If anyone thinks times have changed, they didn't pay attention when DNC staffers referred to Latino voters as &quot;Taco Bowls&quot;, or when HRC called Black youth &quot;Super Predators&quot; in 1996. HRC staffers referred to Sanders supporters as basement dwellers and plotted to use his Jewish faith against him in the primaries! They are talking about their own voter base here people!!! I am not saying that Democratic voters are this way, I am saying the DNC is. I am saying the Democratic politicians are this way. Just because one political party does some bad stuff, doesn't mean their voter base condones it. George W. Bush did some crappy stuff, doesn't mean I am cool with it just because I vote Republican, the same can be said for Democrats. HRC and the Clinton foundation sold American policy to the highest bidder, that doesn't mean her voters support political corruption. We all know that we never get the best possible candidate to vote for, we can only hope that we can live with giving them our vote. A growing number of Republican leaders and their voter base oppose Trump. Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>My god where to begin. First no one called you a racist or bigot. HOWEVER, and this is a big however for a reason. The Republican party as an entity has been racist and bigoted in it's modern form. It's made it a key political strategy to court racists and bigots. And yes it sucks for the other Christians and Republicans out there but that is the bed they made. There ARE people out there in both categories who do want to see lgbt literally killed. One of them was banned from visiting at least one country in Africa because of his rallying cry that LGBT need to die. Back during the fight about the display of the popular Confederate battle flag on government property, one of the many many many a-historical and outright lying done to attempt to defend the displays was to bullshit low information citizens, and sadly there are a lot of them, about the history of the parties and the shift that happened with the Southern Strategy. So when I see someone attempt to trot out that same story I automatically get suspicious of that person. Because really what they are saying with that is, &quot;I think you're so stupid I'm going to tell you a half truth at best in order to manipulate your thinking.&quot; And know what happens to the Democrats, as much as I distrust those elements that are becoming far too cozy with business? They get called out on their shit by their own. And please stop, not a damn person is preventing you from expression your opinion and your call of how silenced you are is doubly insulting because it not only is a false statement, it mocks people who actually are or have been silenced on an institutional level. What's happening to you is a rather capitalist notion in a sense. The turn of phrase being the &quot;marketplace of ideas.&quot; and in that so called market place opinions, etc will be critiqued.<br /> <br /> You made a thread and got responses and your response was &quot;I'm going to take my ball and go home.&quot; You are entitled to do that, you are not entitled to falsely claim your are being silenced.<br /> <br /> When a creationist is shut down by a biologist,etc they're not being silenced, when that nutjob &quot;historian&quot; gets his books pulled because his publishing company finds he's lying about Thomas Jefferson he's not being silenced. The push back against what is essentially the &quot;Why wont you tolerate my intolerance.&quot; isn't silencing people. It's the exercising of the principal that your right to swing your fist ends where the other person's nose exists because people have the right to go about their day without being assaulted. A lesson obviously a man like Trump neither respects nor understands. And now it's at the point that he's claiming if he loses that it's been rigged, that his voters need to stalk voting areas in order to watch out for refugees, immigrants, non white people in general,etc. That they have to be watched for potential voter fraud, people at his rallies outright calling for sedition, revolution, assassinations. This happened because the Republican party actively courted that sort of thinking. It didn't magically spring out of Zeus's proverbial head fully formed. The Republican party and those that claim that title have to own that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:59:17-07:00","id":987899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was us the people, not the republicans who picked him.. Heck the party on several times, looked like they were going to DENY him the nod, till they started seeing the backlash from voters...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely correct. The Republican political class does not actually believe in the rhetoric they've used for decades and is only now waking up to how their voting base does not stand for it. It's how Trump cleaved through the primary process, always capturing a majority of every major constituency that make up the base in polls. It's a long video, but I'd recommend Mark Blyth's talk on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bkm2Vfj42FY\" target=\"_blank\">Trumpism</a> for a greater understanding of the movement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why i have never understood why so many blacks ARE life long democrats.. unless its cause of all the free stuff, or the schools are NOT teaching any of that in history classes..</div> </div> </div> </div>This, on the other hand, is bizarre. There was a realignment in United States politics where the southern Democrats, or Dixiecrats, split off and joined the Republican party over the Civil Rights movement. The Republican party of today is <i>not</i> the &quot;party of Lincoln&quot; with regards to civil rights and every minority is well aware of that, which is how they can <a href=\"http://fivethirtyeight.com/features/trump-is-in-fourth-place-among-black-voters/\" target=\"_blank\">poll below third-parties for support from the African-American community.</a> It isn't about &quot;free stuff&quot; it's about how Republicans keep getting caught red-handed engaging in <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/post-politics/wp/2016/10/15/group-accuses-mike-pence-of-voter-suppression-after-state-police-raid-registration-program-in-indiana/\" target=\"_blank\">voter supression</a>. <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2016/07/30/opinion/north-carolinas-voting-restrictions-struck-down-as-racist.html\" target=\"_blank\">Again</a> and <a href=\"http://www.rollingstone.com/politics/features/the-gops-stealth-war-against-voters-w435890\" target=\"_blank\">again</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voting_Rights_Act_of_1965\" target=\"_blank\">again</a> conservatives attack civil rights for minorities and they remember who is responsible when it's time to vote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pot, Meet Kettle.. You claim trump called over the haters.. BUT i have not heard a single trump supporter spew anywhere near the level of hatred and venom towards someone else as i just read... PERIOD.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.alternet.org/election-2016/10-hate-crimes-inspired-donald-trumps-hateful-rhetoric\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a list. Or <a href=\"https://twitter.com/AdamParkhomenko/status/786472154661527552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> for a video compilation for the standard stuff we see recorded from Trump rallies. Hate speech towards minorities is one of the defining frightening moments of this crazy election.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:06:33-07:00","id":987901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987891#post987891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and doesn't seem to understand that the President is not the CEO of America, nor does it change the fact that he has driven multiple companies into bankruptcy..</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair this is a problem also from the voting public, people in general have a poor understanding of what a president does and power does he exactly has, thinking of presidency as monarchy. Not just trump or hilary supporters but even on the previous election with obama it was the same think. People though he was gonna change everything, and feel cheated when he didnt manage that.<br /> <br /> Is not like the president can just go up when he assumes office and go &quot;okay, plebs im president now so let this are gonna be the new laws&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:23:14-07:00","id":987906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was us the people, not the republicans who picked him.. Heck the party on several times, looked like they were going to DENY him the nod, till they started seeing the backlash from voters...</div> </div> </div> </div>And this was a mistake. The Republican Party should not be a group that bows down to the mob. Republican leadership should have simply said, &quot;Sorry. We will not accept a racist, sexist bigot to represent our organization to the world. This is not who Republicans are, this is not what we believe in, and this is not someone we will stand shoulder-to-shoulder with. To those who support racism and sexism, I'm sorry but this is not the political party for you. If that means you will not vote for us, so be it. The morals of our party and what we stand for are not something we will lightly throw away.&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead they did the opposite, allowing their party to be used as a platform so that a racist, sexist bigot could spread his hateful messages to the world. And now Republicans are struggling because they have linked themselves to and supported Trump, they are facing a backlash from voters. Unfortunately this election has demonstrated that the Republican Party is simply a party of opportunists without overriding principles - a group who is more than happy to chuck their morals to the side if they think it can mean getting a few more votes.<br /> <br /> If there is anything I have taken away from this election, it's that John Kasich was the only Republican in the primary has principles and a backbone. He, alone, has refused to taint himself or his beliefs by embracing Trump, and while I don't agree with everything he says, I respect the guy. If Kasich ever runs for an office where I have the ability to vote for him, he's got every vote I can give him.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Have to correct myself, Jeb Bush also refused to endorse Trump. I can respect that but regardless, he ain't gonna be getting any votes from me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-15-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:32:11-07:00","id":987911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pot, Meet Kettle.. You claim trump called over the haters.. BUT i have not heard a single trump supporter spew anywhere near the level of hatred and venom towards someone else as i just read... PERIOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no. I hate the sexist, racist, bigot. I'M THE REAL MONSTER.<br /> <br /> Less sarcastically, if you haven't seen trump supporters spewing worse hatred than me, then you haven't been paying attention.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:37:33-07:00","id":987915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987901#post987901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair this is a problem also from the voting public, people in general have a poor understanding of what a president does and power does he exactly has, thinking of presidency as monarchy. Not just trump or hilary supporters but even on the previous election with obama it was the same think. People though he was gonna change everything, and feel cheated when he didnt manage that.<br /> <br /> Is not like the president can just go up when he assumes office and go &quot;okay, plebs im president now so let this are gonna be the new laws&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, people get upset when presidents don't uphold their campaign promises, and it's like... You don't think he <i>tried</i>? He had a plan. It might have even worked, if he'd been able to put it into action. Or it might not have, we'll never know. Because no plan survives contact with Congress. What worries me is that we've got multiple Supreme Court Justices poised to retire soon, and <i>they</i> do have a huge impact on policy. And since the President appoints them, I don't want the person making <i>that</i> decision to be a political amateur with a mind full of hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-15-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:48:24-07:00","id":987920,"title":"","content":"I'm of the same opinon, but as a generally pro-gun guy, I don't want Hillary making that call either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pot, Meet Kettle.. You claim trump called over the haters.. BUT i have not heard a single trump supporter spew anywhere near the level of hatred and venom towards someone else as i just read... PERIOD. </div> </div> </div>Which of you two talked about running over protestors scant weeks ago? Matthew 7:3-5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:20:36-07:00","id":987935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we should start rewarding cheating, lying and corruption?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necesarily but society will start to condone it. Think about how &quot;inmoral&quot; things that would have crushed a politician carrer 10 or 20 years ago now would be but a blip on their carrers. Eventually we gonna have to divorce morality from the presidency and focus on their actual capacity.<br /> <br /> Because at the end of the day, a president has to attend to the majority of the country but nothing says that what that mayority wants has to be morally correct (assuming that morally correct is a objective value which so far it isnt).<br /> <br /> I personally dont care if the president is good person or not but that he can push the country to economic and social wellbeing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987915#post987915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What worries me is that we've got multiple Supreme Court Justices poised to retire soon, and <i>they</i> do have a huge impact on policy. And since the President appoints them, I don't want the person making <i>that</i> decision to be a political amateur with a mind full of hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, thats another matter entirely. But something that worries me is how little coverage/importance democracies give to supreme courts appointments and how much it does give to presidents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987920#post987920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of you two talked about running over protestors scant weeks ago? Matthew 7:3-5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think i did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-15-2016, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:39:56-07:00","id":987942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987935#post987935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, thats another matter entirely. But something that worries me is how little coverage/importance democracies give to supreme courts appointments and how much it does give to presidents.</div> </div> </div> </div>As important as they are, they are usually just a going over of previous decisions and for the most part not the type of sensationalism that gets a lot of viewers. Clarence Thomas was probably the most modern exception and that was in the early 90s.<br /> <br /> And this is a surprisingly volatile election year. A potential presidential candidate stated they believed the pyramids were grain silos. One accused Ted Cruz's father of being involved with the assassination of JFK. And after repeatedly mocking and insulting them, a number of these candidates, after dropping out, seemed to throw out all their disagreements with Trump and sided with him. As has been noted several times above, the Republican party has been grooming a certain kind of constituent for decades, and did not seem prepared at all when they made their desires heard.<br /> <br /> Someone mentioned a liberal bias about the news, and pointed out a 'savaging' of Palin. I think with her, Trump, and way back during Quayle, it was more an issue of the person saying something spectacularly wrong, stupid, or considered inappropriate. Even Gore was mocked for his statements about the creation of the Internet, and in that case he was correct, it just seemed hard to believe to most people. Alternatively people like John McCain and even Dick Chaney are treated with respect, for the most part. But Palin and Trump have a speaking style that revolves around provoking loud reactions from their crowd, without thought for people outside of it. They throw out some declarations, find out what gets the loudest results, and follow that vein until it ends. And pleasing those crowds can often lead to what some people call 'putting their foot in their mouth,' and others 'wildly offensive,' and reporters probably just consider a great news day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:45:02-07:00","id":987947,"title":"","content":"Given Trump is perfectly happy to associate his business with indentured servitude that borders on pure slavery, let alone his repeated promises to gut the 1st Amendment, why do you think he'll actually care about the 2nd Amendment if he was in office as was suddenly at risk of &quot;2nd Amendment solutions,&quot; being fired at him?<br /> <br /> Also the whole &quot;pro-gun&quot; means voting against the Democrats thing remains nonsense. The majority of pro-gun identifying individuals support universal background checks, closing loopholes that make it easier for criminals to get guns, and all sorts of laws that aren't going to stop law abiding citizens from owning guns for whatever legal reasons they want. The Democrats are the ones pushing for things most pro-gun Americans want, and the Republicans are blocking it.<br /> <br /> The NRA claims that a functional federal firearms background check and registration system will magically turn into the government taking your guns away, and suddenly you need to vote for the people that don't actually represent your ideals because Reasons nobody can actually explain coherently.<br /> <br /> Look at the horrible nanny-state gun-haters of Australia with there super strict anti-gun laws... despite their country still having lots of guns and gun owners that have to deal with such horrible burdens as, &quot;if you want a carry license for your pistol, you have to belong to a shooting club of some sort and shot in at least one of their events per year,&quot; and, &quot;every few years the police will schedule an appointment to inspect your gun safe/etc. which can't be used to seize your guns in the moment even if you're in violation unless you do something stupid like aim them at the cops for showing up when you asked them to.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:00:54-07:00","id":987980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987869#post987869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why i have never understood why so many blacks ARE life long democrats.. unless its cause of all the free stuff, or the schools are NOT teaching any of that in history classes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No, that level of racism does not go without a response. Take a week off, and if you come back and make another statement like this the suspension will be made permanent.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T19:42:37-07:00","id":988069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987942#post987942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As important as they are, they are usually just a going over of previous decisions and for the most part not the type of sensationalism that gets a lot of viewers. Clarence Thomas was probably the most modern exception and that was in the early 90s.<br /> <br /> And this is a surprisingly volatile election year. A potential presidential candidate stated they believed the pyramids were grain silos. One accused Ted Cruz's father of being involved with the assassination of JFK. And after repeatedly mocking and insulting them, a number of these candidates, after dropping out, seemed to throw out all their disagreements with Trump and sided with him. As has been noted several times above, the Republican party has been grooming a certain kind of constituent for decades, and did not seem prepared at all when they made their desires heard.<br /> <br /> Someone mentioned a liberal bias about the news, and pointed out a 'savaging' of Palin. I think with her, Trump, and way back during Quayle, it was more an issue of the person saying something spectacularly wrong, stupid, or considered inappropriate. Even Gore was mocked for his statements about the creation of the Internet, and in that case he was correct, it just seemed hard to believe to most people. Alternatively people like John McCain and even Dick Chaney are treated with respect, for the most part. But Palin and Trump have a speaking style that revolves around provoking loud reactions from their crowd, without thought for people outside of it. They throw out some declarations, find out what gets the loudest results, and follow that vein until it ends. And pleasing those crowds can often lead to what some people call 'putting their foot in their mouth,' and others 'wildly offensive,' and reporters probably just consider a great news day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the collapse of the Republican Party is easily the most fascinating and worrying bit of politics at least since the failure of the McGovern candidacy. The big tent policy of the GOP have created <i>very</i> strange bedfellows. You have economic conservatives who are likely to be nominally in support of or at least ambivalent to social liberalism sitting alongside cultural and social conservatives who rely on government assistance to get by. Social and culture warriors are openly hateful of the &quot;establishment&quot;, and the moneyed backers of the party hardly veil their hatred for the religious fanatics in their party. Social and economic conservatives would <i>love</i> to court the largely conservative Latinx community, but the vicious racism and xenophobia of their cultural contemporaries makes that next to impossible. It used to be a marriage of convenience. The Republicans had a smaller constituent base, but they managed to stay competitive because they were unified. Republicans would vote Republican all the way down the ticket regardless of grievances they had. But that mish-mash of polarizing and often internally adversarial policies was just too much to sustain. The problem is, when they're no longer unified, any of these given groups is revealed to be an impotent minority. They only have polling power when they're voting together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:12:14-07:00","id":988085,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and reconciling that is going to be hard. More conservative candidates are going to be as hard to push to the entire crowd as more extreme candidates. I suppose it's why the Republicans maintain such a hold on smaller, local elections. You can just sell yourself to the constituency, for now, and not worry about what people in cities in other states think.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's going to be possible for them to stay the course. And their choices are so weird for the past few elections. Palin as vice, Romney, and a whole legion of people this time around. I can't imagine what's going to happen, because I don't see them dividing into a 'rich people party.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:25:49-07:00","id":988091,"title":"","content":"That's actually another reason to go with the more &quot;insider&quot; candidate this year over a wildcard like Trump. 2016's election really isn't going to matter beyond the Supreme court. The chance for actual change (regardless of what direction you think change needs to go in) is 2020, when the next census is up and the gerrymandering game is going to start all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:31:01-07:00","id":988206,"title":"","content":"Maybe my level of English isn't enough to tell all things I want to say. Sorry if sometime my words are wrong.<br /> <br /> I would like a new Ronald Reagan. I don't trust Donal Trump too much, he may be too impulsive for a post of historical proportions, but I don't trust Hillary Clinton at all. Not only about her ideas, but she may be mentally insane. Barack Husseim Obama has been a second Jimmy Carter, or worse. <br /> <br /> Sorry, I am too worried about war at Ucrania, Putin threating with a third world war, jihadism at door of Europe (they want to recover al-Andalus, Spain, my land), China wishing to invade her neighbour waters... but Barack Obama was too busy about gender in the toilet and Hillary conspiring because Christianity is too bothersome for her. <br /> <br /> Northamerican military technology hasn't been updated enough and now Russia and China think they can face NATO forces. What if Putin order invading European East, or Moroccan king send troops to Ceuta and Melilla, two Spanish cities (from centuries ago) in North Africa, North Korea bombard Seul, Iran get nuclear weapons to blackmail thei