 enjoy having the right to marry and I'd like to add the right to be employed to that list. That'd be <i>swell</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Republican platform this election is kind of a tire fire, to be honest. It tacitly supports conversion therapy, which is an unholy and unforgivable blight upon this world. Oh and it states that republican senators will continue to refuse to do their job by not appointing a supreme court justice, which is nice.<br /> <br /> They also want to privatize Social Security- because exposing our retired elders to market forces is the <i>best </i>possible way to ensure they get the money they deserve! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I could go on all day, but to put it shortly: To me, most of the Republican positions fall somewhere between misguided and abominable.<br /> <br /> The alternatives aren't much better to be honest. The Green Party is absorbing the left's crazy anti-science groups; generally desperately scraping for votes. Oh and Libertarians. Their policies seem out-right neglectful to me.<br /> <br /> I mean, Johnson thinks the best way to help poor kids go to college is to remove federally backed loans, based on the belief that the magic of market forces will lower the price of college to a manageable level; not (as college education is basically required for any non-service job) just result in tons of people suddenly being forced away from higher-paying jobs. Supporting a poor-stay-poor ethic doesn't quite seem like a good idea, but other people may have different opinions.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the way Libertarians seem to want to run government, I'd expect a the poverty rate to sky-rocket while the suddenly laissez faire federal government allows half the nation to reverse decades of social progress.<br /> <br /> I mean, I know the only think keeping my sexuality from being outright illegal is probably the threat of the Feds hanging above the collective heads of my state like the fist of an angry god.<br /> <br /> So I'm voting Democrat because they're the non-crazy alternative to <i>seceding away </i>my basic human rights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:42:46-07:00","id":988245,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread reminds me why I hate American politics so fucking much.<br /> <br /> Okay were, to begin.<br /> <br /> Trump is in idiot who will say anything that pops into his head. So no I don't believe he sexually assaulted anyone, I'm also found out stuff about some of the claims against them, that strongly indicate they're bogus, including one where the witness said it didn't happen.<br /> <br /> Still this is a man who in court took out his birth certificate to prove his mother wasn't an orungatung, who says stupid things so often its too long to list here, and who picked a homophobic bigot as his running mate. I also predict Trump will piss so many people off in Congress and the Senate that the American government will largely be crippled. When the best arguements from Trump that I hear are he'll be powerless because both parties hate him, that's a shitty endorsement.<br /> <br /> But he opposes the TTP so at least he has that.<br /> <br />