They don't forgive us the Spanish reconquest, &quot;la Reconquista&quot;. My intention isn't inciting hate againts islam, becuase it isn't only morally questionable but also a great strategic mistake. I would rather to send the message the true religous piety has to respect the human dignity. Showing hostility againt all Muslims is wrong, because they will think they have to support radical Muslims because they are threatened by islamophobic radicals. It is better to say to those peaciful Muslims they are also threatened by radicals because these considere those as bad Muslims, and to survive they have to help us againts our common enemy. I defend the message &quot;if you are a good neighbour, and I will respect you, I will not bother you. I am only againts who cause troubles and don't respect coexistence rules&quot;.<br /> <br /> * Sorry but I can't notice when my words are too nasty. My intuition and social skills aren't so good like yours, and because I have suffered psychological abuse (school bulling and media anti-clericalism) I can't understand where it the precise limit between correct criticing and too offending.<br /> <br /> * I agree we have to understand the radical islamists' minds, like the police who studies criminal psychology to learn to anticipate future criminal actions, but to understand the enemy doesn't mean justify it. Of course they think they are victims of historical injustices like crusades or colonialism, and they have got the right, the duty, of punish us for our crimes, our sins. Don't allow them win the propaganda war. Yes, we need self-criticism and admiting we aren't perfect, we aren't saints, we have to correct and improve a lot of things, but that doesn't mean we are the only ones who have to feel guilty. and they have nothing to be ashamed or regretful. Knowing enemy and his reasons isn't excusing his actions.<br /> <br /> In the right time the quill is more powerful than the sword, the words may be more powerful than the weapons, and we have to face the propaganda war and to take part in the counternarrative againts terrorist speech.<br /> <br /> Another times the only possible diplomacy to avoid start a fight is smiling and saying &quot;go ahead, make my day&quot;, because showing to be too peace-loving really cause the fight because they think you are too coward and weak to face them. Do remember the 1983 Munich agreement had to have avoid the second world war, but it didn't it.<br /> <br /> We agree generalizing is wrong, not all aliens are criminals, nor, for example, all Spanish people like bullfighting or dancing sevillanas (folk ballet from South Spain). But we have to talk about &quot;rotten appels&quot;, not all the apples in the basket are rotten, but we have to avoid somebody may be hurt by those bad fruits. When we want to talk about the &quot;bad seeds&quot; doesn't mean we think all from certain are evil.<br /> <br /> * When you are going to vote, remeber we don't need higher salaries but higher purchasing power, (higher salaries don't work if prices raise more by the inflaction) and we will got this if taxes are reduced by means of stop wrong public expense. They poverty isn't caused by all businessmen, but by bad managers in the goverments. We don't need a fish everyday, but our own fishing rod. Don't trust who promises a babysitter state. The state with power to give all you want also can take away all you own. We don't need free food and home like a canary bird in a jail. They want you to be too dependent of the govement to controll you. We have got right to public services, but they aren't really free, because we are paying them with our taxes. We have to elect the best one to manage the money of the taxes. <br /> <br /> Don't allow be manipulated by means of half-truths and feelings(desire, fear, pride or rancor). Forget thoses nonenenses about &quot;listen your heart&quot;, but listen the voice of reason. Learn to recognize the falaccies and prejudices. contrast all different points of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-17-2016, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:00:20-07:00","id":988815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Amazing Athethist really nails it on the head. Trump and the Clinton dynamic duo are all rotten people, but people on both sides are being hypocrits.<br /> <br /> The Democracts are happy to believe the rape, sexual assault, and pedo allegationas against Trump, while brushing aside the same thing for Bill Clinton, as well as the domestic violence scandal that Hillary was accused of by a former secret service agent.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Trumpites (because Trump has largely replaced or driven out the republicans), happy believe every allegation of rape, pedo, ect... Against Bill Clinton or Domestic Violence ect... Against Hillary.<br /> <br /> None of its been proven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:09:09-07:00","id":988820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ok1Gd0CQsiM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ok1Gd0CQsiM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Ok1Gd0CQsiM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Ok1Gd0CQsiM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Diane Davidson analyisis the Donald Trump leaked tape.<br /> <br /> I have to be honest, it clear from the context and bill bush's laughter that they weren't being serious, why is everyone acting like it was some dead serious confession?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a model gropes a 100 random men without so much as an introduction and the media isn't concerned in the slightest. I don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:58:24-07:00","id":988841,"title":"","content":"&quot;A few days before the fall of Constantinople to the armies of Ottoman jihad, some six centuries ago, a strange debate was taking place inside the imperial city. Constantinople then had a very loud senate, stubborn theologians, and merciless philosophers. It was the heir to Greco-Roman civilization, but also host to hot debates \u2014 so hot that they effectively isolated the city\u2019s elites from the realities of then-world politics. The political establishment of the Eastern Rome was consumed in complex rhetoric \u2014 what historians would later call \u201cByzantine debate.\u201d Just days before the city fell to the Islamic armies that were surrounding its walls, a rabid debate was splitting the lawmakers and their respective intellectuals. Was it about how to defend the state, or how to protect the people? Neither. The sultan and his men were perplexed as to what was on their enemies\u2019 agenda. He had to send spies for intelligence. Upon their return from the mission, they delivered the secret. The political establishment of the Byzantines was sharply split over a major question which superseded everything else, including the marching jihad. And that summa matter was: What is the sex of the angels? Are they males or females?<br /> <br /> Thousands of mujahedeen was closing in from all directions, yet in the minds of the most advanced elites of the Mediterranean, determining the gender of the angels was more important&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> We are in the beggining of the second cold war, the third world war could start in the next years. Do you think it's the best time to talk about the candidates' private life and sins? For me that is like debating about the gender of the angels during the previous days of the fall of Constantinople. People should be talking about serious issues like for example:<br /> <br /> - how to fix economy(lesser taxes and the right reduction of expenses by goverment, lesser rules to create new business),<br /> - how stopping political corruption by secret lobbys, govement's favors to corporations for revolving doors. (It's a true democracy if all parties are only a group of dummies who obey instructions dictated by secret lobbys)<br /> - North Korea and Iran's nuclear menaces.<br /> - war in Ucrania<br /> - drug traffickers and organized crime trying suborn politicals,<br /> - making aware youngest generations about venereal diseases, and avoid they can join to young gangs.<br /> - the university bubble (people who haven't could complete the major but they are in debt too much, or with the diploma but they can't earn money to pay the studies debts),<br /> - plans of social engineerings to controll people's opinion,<br /> - media oligopoly that try to impose the single thought. (take careful about the argument to moderation or fallacy of the middle ground). <br /> - abuses by some health insuraces who don't want to pay certain operations (like Denzel Washinton in the movie &quot;John Q&quot;).<br /> - counternarrative. stopping enemy propaganda what shows USA like the new evil American empire (Spain was the previous &quot;evil&quot; American empire), guilty of all the injustices in the world and liable to cause terrorist groups' rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 10-17-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:37:26-07:00","id":988853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988815#post988815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/Bgmh4nx7xnE</a><br /> <br /> Amazing Athethist really nails it on the head. Trump and the Clinton dynamic duo are all rotten people, but people on both sides are being hypocrits.<br /> <br /> The Democracts are happy to believe the rape, sexual assault, and pedo allegationas against Trump, while brushing aside the same thing for Bill Clinton, as well as the domestic violence scandal that Hillary was accused of by a former secret service agent.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Trumpites (because Trump has largely replaced or driven out the republicans), happy believe every allegation of rape, pedo, ect... Against Bill Clinton or Domestic Violence ect... Against Hillary.<br /> <br /> None of its been proven.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the entire point of Trump bringing up Bill Clinton's accusers, to cause this exact false equivalence. The Democrats brush aside those allegations right now because they are not pertinent to <b>Hillary</b> Clinton's fitness for President; they're the fault of her husband, not her. The Secret Service officer's book runs into the problem that the author wasn't a Secret Service agent, making a lot of his stories suspect as fabrications since he appears to be using the layperson's confusion with his junior role to pretend he ever served in the Presidential detail. Juanita Broderrick's complaint against Hillary is that she was thanked for her work at a fundraiser and found that sinister, taking it as a threat to remain silent. There are similar exaggerations with the arguments that Hillary &quot;laughed at a rape victim&quot;; we have the audio for the interview (<a href=\"http://www.factcheck.org/2016/06/clintons-1975-rape-case/\" target=\"_blank\">found here</a>) where she's speaking to a reporter. In recounting details she laughs at the validity of polygraph tests after her client passed one, at the prosecutor for stonewalling her request to see evidence, and at the point discussing forensics on underwear samples with the judge. She never laughed at the victim, nor did she volunteer for the case, as has been claimed repeatedly by the Trump campaign.<br /> <br /> Bill Clinton likely committed sexual assault and if he were running for president today he'd be disqualified by several of the other allegations which are more credible.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we have an audio brag about sexual assault by Donald Trump followed by a dozen or so allegations that he really does do the things he says he does. His defense has been to find a self-confessed pimp of underage boys to British politicians to serve as his &quot;witness&quot; (whose story both gets the year of the assault wrong AND places him on first-class flight to the US at the age of 17) or to attack his accusers as not pretty enough for him to have groped. And, of course, the Amazing Athiest is the absolute worst kind of Internet talking head MRA to get information from on this subject. Or any subject, he's kind of famously an idiot. I know Mr. (&quot;<a href=\"http://freethoughtblogs.com/pharyngula/2012/02/08/the-not-so-amazing-atheist-self-immolates/\" target=\"_blank\">I will make you a rape victim if you don't fuck off</a>&quot;) is the last person I'd go to for discussing proper conduct in society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","user":"Shinjo","date":". 10-17-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:11:19-07:00","id":988860,"title":"","content":"@Luis_Carlos, I am getting profoundly tired of you dismissing gender as an unimportant subject every other post you make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:24:16-07:00","id":988917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988860#post988860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Luis_Carlos, I am getting profoundly tired of you dismissing gender as an unimportant subject every other post you make.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;&lt;points to the Ignore feature&gt;&gt; I've found it amazingly useful when it comes to his posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:32:26-07:00","id":988950,"title":"","content":"Look at it in context. He was discussing the Byzantine Empire about to be attacked and the most important thing they could think of to discuss was the gender of Angels. There were more pressing matters at hand than theological discussions, that's the point he was trying to make.<br /> <br /> \u200bHe's saying that a similar situation exists now, that we are debating unimportant issues in comparison to the major issues at hand. When your house is on fire you don't discuss what color to paint the walls.<br /> <br /> I disagree with him on taxes as supply side economics has been proven repeatedly to be a failure at building a middle class and alleviating poverty, and we in the US have seen what happens to the national debt when you cut taxes while simultaneously starting a two front war.<br /> <br /> I disagree with his statement that America shouldn't be taken to task for many of the problems we face in the world today. We destabilized the Middle East, not Russia, not China, not anyone fucking else. We created the problem and need to take responsibility and ownership of it. Both parties have dirty hands here, but one actively pushed the lie that Iraq had nuclear weapons and was an imminent threat that had to be invaded. I keep that thought in mind every single time I hear people ranting about &quot;the nuclear threat of Iran&quot;. Now conservatives rant about 10,000 Syrian refugees (soon to increase to about 50k) coming to the US. If you don't like the idea of refugees from war torn countries you shouldn't support your country creating those refugees through direct or indirect action.<br /> I keep seeing conservative memes about Clinton arming ISIS, but what I don't see in those memes is that those supposed ISIS members are the rebels fighting Assad in Syria, the same rebels that John McCain and Lindsay Graham were calling &quot;good people&quot; who needed to be armed by the US to fight for their freedom. I don't see a lot of concern that the rebels the CIA are arming are fighting the rebels the US Army has supplied. It's a complex fucking shitstorm, but it's real easy to just go &quot;it's Hillary's fault&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo all these discussions about the presidential candidates lives and personal matters ARE relevant, because it speaks to their decision making ability and we don't want to give the most influential political position in the world to some incompetent jackass who is going to fuck the job up again. Been there, done that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:42:09-07:00","id":988956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988802#post988802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I make you remember Spain, my land, is one of the main targets of islamic terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of jihadist terrorism takes place in the Muslim world, closely followed by Israel, then all of the West combined.<br /> <br /> As well, Interpol's data makes it abundantly clear that the vast majority of terror attacks in Europe are domestic attacks, and mostly from groups like ETA, not external groups like ISIL. Despite the horrific attacks recently, Europe is still experiencing much less terrorism than it used to because of the successful nullification of separatist terrorist groups.<br /> <br /> Spain might be a big propaganda target for ISIL and similar groups, but that doesn't mean it's actually a main target (the idea of them having a main target is misleading, because they're largely working on just getting whoever they can to commit acts of terror in their home countries).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't forgive us the Spanish reconquest, &quot;la Reconquista&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The Crusades in general are a major cultural touchstone for such groups. They use the Crusades to paint the last thousand years as a war of Christians trying to wipe out Muslims.<br /> <br /> As you mention in your next post though, the much more effective recruitment is because of Spanish colonialism in north Africa. La Reconquista is just used to connect this over the generations as an on-going conflict; so the more recent events look worse as they're woven together with old events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My intention isn't inciting hate againts islam, becuase it isn't only morally questionable but also a great strategic mistake. </div> </div> </div>How about not trying to compare Muslims to fictional barbarians and monsters then?<br /> <br /> Even if your intent was to call peaceful Muslims the Wildlings fleeing the radical fanatic White Walkers, you're calling the peaceful Muslims a bunch of raiding barbarians that loot and pillage European/Westeros villages.<br /> <br /> Maybe just skip the metaphors and such? Or at least spend a lot more time on thinking them through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My intuition and social skills aren't so good like yours, and because I have suffered psychological abuse (school bulling and media anti-clericalism) I can't understand where it the precise limit between correct criticing and too offending. </div> </div> </div>I don't want to down play anyone's experiences... but this is a RPG forum. I'm fairly confident that if we did a poll, the vast majority of us were bullied as nerds/geeks/etc. Trying to compare there being anti-Christian media out there to the psychological trauma of abuse is frankly absurd. The Preacher comics and TV show are not abuse. Being shamed in front of your class for bad spelling because you don't write one of the names of G-D out properly as a way to honor the commandment to not take the Lord's name in vain? That's abuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another times the only possible diplomacy to avoid start a fight is smiling and saying &quot;go ahead, make my day&quot;, because showing to be too peace-loving really cause the fight because they think you are too coward and weak to face them. Do remember the [1938] Munich agreement had to have avoid the second world war, but it didn't it. </div> </div> </div>The Munich Agreement has pretty much no bearing on modern day terrorism. It would be more relevant in a discussion of Russia's military actions in Ukraine, but it seems that NATO is in no mood for a Munich Agreement over it... so lessons learned?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When you are going to vote, remeber we don't need higher salaries but higher purchasing power, (higher salaries don't work if prices raise more by the inflaction) and we will got this if taxes are reduced by means of stop wrong public expense. </div> </div> </div>The current US minimum wage does not provide enough purchasing power to pay for basic living expenses for most Americans. So yes, we need higher wages with the increased purchasing power that comes with them. Wages alone are not enough, but they can't be allowed to fall below inflation as they have here.<br /> <br /> Reducing taxes isn't going to fix wages that are too low. Fixing the federal tax code will help a little, but that's not the primary thing keeping the average American's purchasing power down.<br /> <br /> And, of course, we'd all have to decide what &quot;wrong&quot; public expenses really are. Both parties want to put lots of money to things the other party says are giant wastes of tax money.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't need a fish everyday, but our own fishing rod. </div> </div> </div>What people usually forget in this, is that if you don't feed the man you're teaching to fish, he starves before he learns to feed himself.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of the money the US collects for such programs go to people that need temporary assistance (sometimes on a long scale, such as public housing which when well funded doesn't really do much for the parents in terms of getting them out of public housing, but makes it much easier for their children to own homes themselves later), or people that cannot full take care of themselves even if they have a &quot;fishing rod&quot; (so the disabled, the elderly, etc.).<br /> <br /> We have a lot of people in programs a lot longer right now, but we're recovering from a major economic catastrophe, which is sort of the point; to make sure that when things go bad, a lot of people don't end up destitute before things can get better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They want you to be too dependent of the govement to controll you. </div> </div> </div>Who is they? Because there's no major political party actually pushing this; and both are doing it in their own small ways anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988841#post988841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are in the beggining of the second cold war, the third world war could start in the next years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely. There isn't the kind of stand off that's an analogy to the Cold War between.... anybody. And a conventional war like the two World Wars seems increasingly unlikely as well.<br /> <br /> If there's going to be a new world wide &quot;hot&quot; war, it's going to be something different than the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think it's the best time to talk about the candidates' private life and sins? </div> </div> </div>If those sins include things like running multiple companies into bankruptcy while declaring yourself a financial genius, when we need to continue to improve our economic recovery? Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - how to fix economy(lesser taxes and the right reduction of expenses by goverment, lesser rules to create new business), </div> </div> </div>Gets talked about plenty. Though it's largely irrelevant to the President because the President doesn't actually handle the federal budget; the Congress does.<br /> <br /> What many people forget is that the federal budget doesn't work like a confirmation hearing where the Congress is simply approving the President's proposal. Initially, the President wasn't even required to submit any budget at all, and was solely responsible for formally requesting a budget from the Congress (a law was passed that requires the President to include a budget proposal later). After that, the Congress can pretty much throw the entire thing out and pass whatever budget they want. The breakdown of this process - where the President, House,and Senate have repeatedly failed to compromise and pass a budget - has been extremely bad for our economy.<br /> <br /> A huge step forward in make our economy work that goes beyond economic ideology is simply getting that process to work again. Compromise budgets that pass and work are better than no budget.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - how stopping political corruption by secret lobbys, govement's favors to corporations for revolving doors. (It's a true democracy if all parties are only a group of dummies who obey instructions dictated by secret lobbys) </div> </div> </div>A huge issue on the left that gets a lot of talk and even if Hillary is a shitty messenger for it, she's going to have to push towards it to maintain party unity. It's pretty much a set Democratic position that any Supreme Court nominee she would appoint has to agree that Citizen's United needs to be overturned in order to decrease dark money in politics.<br /> <br /> The Republicans... remain oddly silent about this as a party. Trump likes to crow about being beyond it because he's rich, but doesn't actually put forward any plan to combat it in the rest of the government (and there's lots of evidence he isn't beyond it just because he's rich).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - North Korea and Iran's nuclear menaces.<br /> - war in Ucrania </div> </div> </div>All have been talked about. North Korea and Ukraine are both basically non-issues because nobody wants to spread the US resources even thinner to take actions beyond maintaining the situations as they are. Iran is basically moot (Trump has said he wouldn't back out of the existing deal even if he thinks its a bad one and would take the first excuse to get out of it without breaking it) as both sides are waiting to see how the current deal goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - drug traffickers and organized crime trying suborn politicals, </div> </div> </div>Not really a big concern in the US, though the issues with the power of drug cartels in other parts of the Americas is a problem. Of course, a lot of the other countries are kind of sick of our &quot;help&quot; in those regards...so neither party has any particularly significant change in policy to propose beyond our current efforts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - making aware youngest generations about venereal diseases, and avoid they can join to young gangs. </div> </div> </div>Wow... these are... two completely different things.<br /> <br /> STI education is a priority for both parties. The issue is far more the fight over other sex education issues and how they might undermine STI education (the general issue is people that want schools to teach kids to just not have sex, but abstinence focused education generally leads to worse rates of STIs and unwanted pregnancies).<br /> <br /> Avoiding joining gangs is not an educational issue. The vast majority of US gang members come from groups with high rates of poverty. Good education is part of a good plan to reduce poverty, but education alone isn't going to solve our gang problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - the university bubble (people who haven't could complete the major but they are in debt too much, or with the diploma but they can't earn money to pay the studies debts), </div> </div> </div>Another major platform issue for the Democrats, and something the Republicans really haven't addressed directly. The Democrats want to directly address the issue by providing debt-free higher education options. The Republicans seem to be arguing that this will solve itself after they fix the economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - plans of social engineerings to controll people's opinion, </div> </div> </div>What exactly is there to discuss?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - media oligopoly that try to impose the single thought. (take careful about the argument to moderation or fallacy of the middle ground). </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trying to impose the single thought&quot; is silly. The media magnates are as politically divided as the rest of us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - abuses by some health insuraces who don't want to pay certain operations (like Denzel Washinton in the movie &quot;John Q&quot;). </div> </div> </div>Again, another Democratic platform position (a major part of Obamacare is requiring health insurance companies to provide coverage for things they used to deny). The Republicans seem to agree it's a problem, but can't offer a good solution without going against their anti-regulation platform; though it is assumed to be part of the &quot;replace&quot; in the &quot;repeal and replace Obamacare&quot; efforts even if it doesn't have any real details on how.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988815#post988815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Democracts are happy to believe the rape, sexual assault, and pedo allegationas against Trump, while brushing aside the same thing for Bill Clinton, as well as the domestic violence scandal that Hillary was accused of by a former secret service agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Trump surrogates have stated directly (about Bill of course) that we should default to believing the victims of sexual abuse by rich and powerful men... so the Trump campaign has saved Democrats from hypocrisy on this one. The Dems get to believe that Bill used his political power to have lots of sleazy extramarital sex, with the three women that represent more serious accusations having all contradicted themselves (even if I'm inclined to believe one despite this since she's remained adamant that this was solely to get away from media attention and being forced to relive her experiences), and they get to believe that Trump regularly used his position of power to sexually assault women. As the Trump campaign has said, just listen to the women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of its been proven. </div> </div> </div>It's not really important to either side really. It's a character argument, not a factual argument. The problem as you note though, is that it's a very stupid character argument for Trump because he ends up compared to Bill who's not his opponent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988820#post988820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diane Davidson analyisis the Donald Trump leaked tape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems... fairly suspect to me. There's a few points in there with some merit, but the overall idea that the tape proves Trump doesn't sexually assault women doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to be honest, it clear from the context and bill bush's laughter that they weren't being serious, why is everyone acting like it was some dead serious confession? </div> </div> </div>I think the bigger outrages are that most people think that joking about sexually assaulting people is a seriously bad thing to do, and that Trump's handling of it has been to do anything but acknowledge that and show contrition. His repeated excuse of &quot;locker room talk,&quot; body shaming his accusers, and accusing his accusers of having political motivations as if he hasn't faced lots of accusations before now, all add up to at a minimum a guy that doesn't really get it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile a model gropes a 100 random men without so much as an introduction and the media isn't concerned in the slightest. I don't get it. </div> </div> </div>Well, first thing, she's a Brazilian that's not running for the US presidency. Second, she was explicitly doing it as a stunt which means regardless of how you feel about her motives or actions, she basically failed at her goals because she wanted media attention and isn't getting it (so maybe we can call that a win for the media in this case?). Third, the media is probably a bit apprehensive about these sorts of viral videos because they've been staged in the past and nobody wants to end up with egg on their face because they reported a woman going on a sexual assault spree that turned out to be a bunch of actors doing a protest video.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:30:18-07:00","id":988996,"title":"","content":"* Have you fett anytime like a jedi of Star War who had to choose between voting senator Palpatine and count Dooku?<br /> <br /> * The gender of the angels in the previous days of the fall of Constatinople is a historical example about people who were too busy with nonenses when more serious and important matters were about to happen. Other example is when in October 1917 the Russia Ortodox Church was talking about the color of the surplice for the ceremones. (they didn't notice the Russia revolution was about to start and change History). My message is losing time with gossips is like talking about the gender of the angels.<br /> <br /> * I don't like the attack in North Carolina GOP office. It has made me to remember the &quot;Kale Borroka&quot; (street fight in Euskera languange), the vandal actions by extreme-left Basque independentist radicals. I don't want to think it is only the tip of the iceberg of the future events.<br /> <br /> * This isn't only about conservative vs liberal ideas. Can you really trust Hillary Clinton? Don't forget the American soldiers who died in Bengashi because an airplane wasn't allowed to be sent to rescue them. <br /> <br /> There are rumors about she is suffering subcortical vascular dementia. <br /> <br /> * What did that Hillary say about &quot;and deep-seated cultural codes, religious beliefs and structural biases have to be changed&quot;? It doesn't sound nice. <br /> <br /> * Most of victims of jihadist terrorism are the own Muslims, and they don't notice this is causing lots of young Muslims start to lose faith. I know this, I don't need you have to make me to remember it.<br /> <br /> Terrorist haven't enough recourses for attacks in Spain. We have experencie fighting against ETA, and after 1975 Green March in the Spanish Sahara, we haven't stopped watching Morocco.<br /> <br /> They think we are in our moment of highest weakness, we are become too stupy, coward, hedonist, corrupt, decayed, by our sins, alcohol, sex, reality shows in the TV, sports, without willpower, guts and capacity of sacrifice to face them. We have go change that and make clear we can suffer, but we will not surrender, and we aren't going to be feel guilty only because enemy propaganda tell we are the evil empire. <br /> <br /> * Crusades weren't an assault, but a failed reconquest, a counterstrike againts Otoman empire. We were the attacked victims. Did you know the famour pirate &quot;Red Beard&quot; really was Otoman? Christian coasts in the Mediterranean sea suffered Sarracen pirates who capture slaves, the men to be eunuch (not all survived the castration) and the women to be concubines in the harems. Wester should thank Spain to have stopped Otoman empire in the battle of Lepante.<br /> <br /> * I like fantasy because it is a softer way to talk about controversial threads. If I can't talk about Spanish heroes againts Otoman pirates, then I will talk about elves againts orcs.<br /> <br /> You can say it is bad taste to show white walkers from &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; like a metaphor about islamic invasion, you have got the right to give your opinion. But now I hope you can understand like I feel when I suposse some fictional religous groups from geek fiction (Fadings Suns rpg, Warhammer 40.000, 7th Sea rpg) are used like an allegory about Catholic Church). <br /> <br /> Sorry if my words may be so &quot;awkward&quot; and annoying. It isn't my intention to offend because I don't enjoy with that. Now you can go to watch a new episode of the TV serie &quot;Preacher&quot;. <br /> <br /> * My level of English isn't enough to give the right answer about any complex matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:54:56-07:00","id":989007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988788#post988788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bAbaddon is a weak third party candidate, your only real choices are Grazz't and Asmodeus. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If either or both candidates came out as being controlled by any of the 3 listed above, I would be more surprised that they <i>actually let that information out</i> then I would be by fact that the demons really exist or that they are in their thrall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:19:26-07:00","id":989015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988206#post988206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, now I am busy. A group of white walkers from beyond the wall of North Westeros have just arrived and Angela Merkel wants to allow them to enter here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Game of Thrones is an interesting place to go for this metaphor given that the Wildlings were refugees who were given lands in Westeros and the people who had a problem with that united under the banner of serial rapist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:30:37-07:00","id":989042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Have you fett anytime like a jedi of Star War who had to choose between voting senator Palpatine and count Dooku?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I have never felt like a member of a semi-monastic group of warrior mystics that as a matter of principle don't participate in civil politics (including voting), that is somehow being forced to choose between voting for a man that seems decent and is a duly elected member of my government and is unknowingly my enemy (I'm assuming this to be the case since we're talking about Senator Palpatine and Count Dooku which implies before Palpatine took over the Senate), and voting for a man that has no official political station and is a known traitor to my order and a known leader of separatist paramilitary forces.<br /> <br /> It's not really a situation any real person's had to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My message is losing time with gossips is like talking about the gender of the angels. </div> </div> </div>And? It's how most Americans of all political stripes feel about the current election. The issue is that, well, most Americans also get bored with deep policy discussions because it's hard to be well informed on a single issue, let alone a dozen of them, and the Trump Reality TV Campaign is exciting.<br /> <br /> In this case the issue isn't the leaders getting distracted, most of them have expressed repeated frustration with needing to campaign in a climate where the public doesn't really want to listen to an academic policy debate, so they have to get into the &quot;gossip&quot; to get elected and then go back to the policy stuff. They know they're being distracted, but as a democracy they don't have much of a choice but to cater to the people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't like the attack in North Carolina GOP office. </div> </div> </div>I don't want to spend time with anyone that does like the idea of firebombing the office of rival political parties. Nobody should like this, and I hope they find and punish the perpetrators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you really trust Hillary Clinton? </div> </div> </div>Trust isn't binary. There are only around six people I absolutely trust on Earth. Everyone else gets some degree of mixed trust.<br /> <br /> Do I trust Hillary to be president? Yes. I don't find any of her mistakes, character flaws, lies, or politics to be overtly malicious, so I trust her to do the job. I'm sure she'll do things I don't like. I'm sure she'll do things immoral or unethical. But that's because so has every other president before her. Point to any US president that's thought to have been a great one, and I'll list a bunch of things that tarnish their records that we overlook.<br /> <br /> Hell, this came up with Bill Clinton. Everybody knew that Bill Clinton liked to sleep around well before he ran for office. He won anyway, because despite trying to have sex with every woman around him, he was good enough at being president his supporters didn't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't forget the American soldiers who died in Bengashi because an airplane wasn't allowed to be sent to rescue them. </div> </div> </div>It's hard to forget something that's not true.<br /> <br /> One of the things that always boggles me about Benghazi myths, is the idea that no reinforcements were sent in response to the attacks when one of the two CIA security operatives that died was part of the reinforcements the CIA sent immediately to the scene (and in fact died because his group voluntarily went into battle ahead of other forces to render aid sooner knowing it was dangerous to do so).<br /> <br /> All of the investigations into the incident have concluded the same thing: no plane was launched because there wasn't a plane to launch that would have helped.<br /> <br /> Americans died because terrorists killed them. By the time the attack started anything that would have helped saved their lives was already too late. The consulate (where the two others were) was overrun too fast for anyone to do anything after it started.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are rumors about she is suffering subcortical vascular dementia. </div> </div> </div>There are also rumors that she's a literal demon sent by Satan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What did that Hillary say about &quot;and deep-seated cultural codes, religious beliefs and structural biases have to be changed&quot;? It doesn't sound nice. </div> </div> </div>I don't care if it doesn't sound nice. It's true. Keep in mind that she was talking about stopping the oppression of women around the world when she said that. I don't think people like the Taliban deserve &quot;nice&quot; language when it comes to condemning their treatment of women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of victims of jihadist terrorism are the own Muslims, and they don't notice this is causing lots of young Muslims start to lose faith. I know this, I don't need you have to make me to remember it. </div> </div> </div>Apparently you do if you want to paint Spain as top target of jihadist terrorists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have go change that and make clear we can suffer, but we will not surrender, and we aren't going to be feel guilty only because enemy propaganda tell we are the evil empire. </div> </div> </div>Why on Earth would you want to change that? An enemy that thinks your weak where you are strong is an enemy doomed to fail (to paraphrase a few dozen military minds).<br /> <br /> Remember that terrorists <b>want you to change</b>. That's the goal of terror. To scare you into doing things differently. You lose the propaganda war when you start to fight them like they fight, so that you become the evil empire. Or if you act with fear instead of purpose and show that you are weak. You win by standing resolute and not letting their violence change your society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crusades weren't an assault, but a failed reconquest, a counterstrike againts Otoman empire. We were the attacked victims. </div> </div> </div>Depending on which definition you want to use there were a lot of Crusades for a lot of reasons. Trying to pin the &quot;victim&quot; status on any one of the major combatants is impossible.<br /> <br /> That said... the Crusades gave birth to the Ottoman Empire. Before the Crusades started there was no Ottoman Empire, and it was born from the power gaps left in Anatolia after the first crusades in the west.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like fantasy because it is a softer way to talk about controversial threads. </div> </div> </div>Which is fine if it works. The problem is you have to think through the comparisons or it doesn't work to make things &quot;softer.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I can't talk about Spanish heroes againts Otoman pirates, then I will talk about elves againts orcs. </div> </div> </div>As long as you're being accurate about your history, nobody is trying to stop you from talking about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can say it is bad taste to show white walkers from &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; like a metaphor about islamic invasion, you have got the right to give your opinion. But now I hope you can understand like I feel when I suposse some fictional religous groups from geek fiction (Fadings Suns rpg, Warhammer 40.000, 7th Sea rpg) are used like an allegory about Catholic Church). </div> </div> </div>No, I don't buy the equivalency. Even if you want to make a case that two things are equally offensive, there is a massive and inherent difference between taking fictional monsters and making them a crude and offensive metaphor for real people that they were never intended to be, and a piece of fiction being used by the creators to make commentary about a real world institution.<br /> <br /> I can empathize with your feelings, but I consistent find them lacking in merit. You hyper-focus on any reason to label something an attack on the Catholic Church and ignore the context. For example Fading Suns' treatment of the Church is fairly even handed, if not pro-Church. The Temple Avesti (aka the demon burning fanatics) are largely considered to radical by the Urth Orthodoxy and the Patriarch himself. The majority of orders within it are highly sympathetic and outright good groups, and the Church is presented as being the sole organization holding humanity together during the dark ages of the setting as well as key fighters in fending off the symbiots. But the whole thing is offensive because they're some burn-them-at-the-stake types in the Church as well?<br /> <br /> Or simple things like Preacher being far more aimed at Protestant doctrines than Catholic ones.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:48:16-07:00","id":989047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you fett anytime like a jedi of Star War who had to choose between voting senator Palpatine and count Dooku?</div> </div> </div> </div>Always. Again, that's modern life. Most of us don't like the options presented to us. Even when the candidates put in front of us aren't ideologues who don't represent our values, there's tough decisions to make regarding policy. Where do we find the balance between liberty and security? How do we cope with the seemingly inevitable transition to a globalist economy? Was Kim Kardashian really robbed? You aren't alone, buddy. This is something we all deal with. That's adulthood for ya.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The gender of the angels in the previous days of the fall of Constatinople is a historical example about people who were too busy with nonenses when more serious and important matters were about to happen. Other example is when in October 1917 the Russia Ortodox Church was talking about the color of the surplice for the ceremones. (they didn't notice the Russia revolution was about to start and change History). My message is losing time with gossips is like talking about the gender of the angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, this thread has kind of zig-zagged around, but your original point was that dwelling on Trump's personal character is as frivolous as debating the gender of angels, right?<br /> <br /> Look, I'm not the kind of person who expects my politicians to be saints. I'll take a savvy opportunist over an earnest and well-intentioned greenhorn any day of the week, but Trump's actions and words are so blatantly ignorant that they reflect just not on what he believes in private but also on his inadequacies as a candidate.<br /> <br /> Promoting the sexual abuse of women is both a reflection of how Trump might handle sexual harassment and gender equality issues, it reflects on the sort of cross-boundaries savvy a politician needs to work across party lines. Telling his believers that he's going to put up a wall and make Mexico pay for it shows both a xenophobic perspective on immigrants and a complete misunderstanding of foreign policy and national economics. Insulting journalists and promoting violence against protesters indicates an utter lack of disdain for the fourth estate and the right to free speech while also indicating a man who is too shallow and unstable to handle the pressure of world affairs. And threatening to imprison your political adversary? That's a play right out of the Idiot's Guide to Tin Pot Dictatorship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the attack in North Carolina GOP office. It has made me to remember the &quot;Kale Borroka&quot; (street fight in Euskera languange), the vandal actions by extreme-left Basque independentist radicals. I don't want to think it is only the tip of the iceberg of the future events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people don't support attacks of radical violence. You aren't alone there. But do attacks on black churches, gay nightclubs, and abortion clinics make you feel the same way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't only about conservative vs liberal ideas. Can you really trust Hillary Clinton? Don't forget the American soldiers who died in Bengashi because an airplane wasn't allowed to be sent to rescue them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can trust Clinton to be a cold pragmatist. All of our Secretaries of State dating back at least to Clinton's presidency lost American citizens to embassy attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are rumors about she is suffering subcortical vascular dementia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poorly substantiated rumors perpetuated by a fringe element in the media with no discernible evidence. These are the same sorts of rumors that suggested Obama was a secret Muslim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did that Hillary say about &quot;and deep-seated cultural codes, religious beliefs and structural biases have to be changed&quot;? It doesn't sound nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sure does sound scary if you take it out of context. However, if you read her <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/clinton-christians-must-deny-faith/\" target=\"_blank\">speech in a manner that wasn't selectively selected to scare individuals</a>, you'd know that she was specifically speaking about countries and governments that use &quot;deep seated cultural cods, religious beliefs and structural biases&quot; to excuse acts of violence against women and girls and deny them basic human rights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I like fantasy because it is a softer way to talk about controversial threads. If I can't talk about Spanish heroes againts Otoman pirates, then I will talk about elves againts orcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it's not, unless your intent is out and out racism and xenophobia. Comparing the Spanish &quot;heroes&quot; to elves (a fantasy race treated as beautiful, wise, and noble) and the Ottomans to orcs (a fantasy race treated as inherently evil) isn't a soter way to talk about controversial threads. It's just a softer way to mask bigotry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can say it is bad taste to show white walkers from &quot;Game of Thrones&quot; like a metaphor about islamic invasion, you have got the right to give your opinion. But now I hope you can understand like I feel when I suposse some fictional religous groups from geek fiction (Fadings Suns rpg, Warhammer 40.000, 7th Sea rpg) are used like an allegory about Catholic Church).</div> </div> </div> </div>Allegory and simile are not necessarily the same thing. You directly comparing an ethnic or religious group to demeaning fictional cultural groups within the context of a real world argument isn't the same as creatives taking elements from real life and repurposing them into allegory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988996#post988996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* My level of English isn't enough to give the right answer about any complex matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if we're misinterpreting your words, but I thought I had a decent handle on what you were saying. Your English is actually pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T17:30:49-07:00","id":989085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989047#post989047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sure does sound scary if you take it out of context. However, if you read her <a href=\"http://www.snopes.com/clinton-christians-must-deny-faith/\" target=\"_blank\">speech in a manner that wasn't selectively selected to scare individuals</a>, you'd know that she was specifically speaking about countries and governments that use &quot;deep seated cultural cods, religious beliefs and structural biases&quot; to excuse acts of violence against women and girls and deny them basic human rights.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always amused me. Hillary was basically calling out Muslim countries that abuse and degrade women. But then people who are, shall we call them &quot;anti-Islamic&quot; get on her case about it even though it's something that, to some degree, both conservatives and liberals recognize as a problem with Islamic nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T18:09:49-07:00","id":989106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=988853#post988853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was the entire point of Trump bringing up Bill Clinton's accusers, to cause this exact false equivalence. The Democrats brush aside those allegations right now because they are not pertinent to <b>Hillary</b> Clinton's fitness for President; they're the fault of her husband, not her. The Secret Service officer's book runs into the problem that the author wasn't a Secret Service agent, making a lot of his stories suspect as fabrications since he appears to be using the layperson's confusion with his junior role to pretend he ever served in the Presidential detail. Juanita Broderrick's complaint against Hillary is that she was thanked for her work at a fundraiser and found that sinister, taking it as a threat to remain silent. There are similar exaggerations with the arguments that Hillary &amp;quot;laughed at a rape victim&amp;quot;; we have the audio for the interview (<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.factcheck.org/2016/06/clintons-1975-rape-case/&amp;quot;]found</a> here[/URL]) where she's speaking to a reporter. In recounting details she laughs at the validity of polygraph tests after her client passed one, at the prosecutor for stonewalling her request to see evidence, and at the point discussing forensics on underwear samples with the judge. She never laughed at the victim, nor did she volunteer for the case, as has been claimed repeatedly by the Trump campaign.<br /> <br /> Bill Clinton likely committed sexual assault and if he were running for president today he'd be disqualified by several of the other allegations which are more credible.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we have an audio brag about sexual assault by Donald Trump followed by a dozen or so allegations that he really does do the things he says he does. His defense has been to find a self-confessed pimp of underage boys to British politicians to serve as his &amp;quot;witness&amp;quot; (whose story both gets the year of the assault wrong AND places him on first-class flight to the US at the age of 17) or to attack his accusers as not pretty enough for him to have groped. And, of course, the Amazing Athiest is the absolute worst kind of Internet talking head MRA to get information from on this subject. Or any subject, he's kind of famously an idiot. I know Mr. (&amp;quot;<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://freethoughtblogs.com/pharyngula/2012/02/08/the-not-so-amazing-atheist-self-immolates/&amp;quot;]I</a> will make you a rape victim if you don't fuck off[/URL]&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> is the last person I'd go to for discussing proper conduct in society.</div> </div> </div> </div> All I know for certain is nobody is has been convicted of anything, but there is alot of mudslinging and accusations going on.<br /> <br /> And I watched the video, which I linked to, he didn't say he sexually assaults anyone. Clearly you disagree, as far as I can see people have dishonestly twisted what he said and the context in which he said them. But I doubt we'll agree on this. <br /> <br /> As for Amazing Atheist, holy shit I had no idea he said that, and he absolutely was in the wrong, flame war or not he crossed the line. I say that as someone who writes twisted fictional porn stories in which various sexual taboos are explored), but yeah saying shit like that right to a rape victim is disgusting.<br /> <br /> But he did apologize, including to the person who he said it to and has since fundraised hundreds of thousands dollars for little girls third world to help them. So I think he's done his pence and his jack assery does nothing to change the points he made in the video. His arguements stand on its own merits.<br /> <br /> I hate trigger warning, but I'm still giving you a heads up he talks about what he wrote, which is some pretty fucked up shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do understand why you were horrified by what he said, I just believe as horrible as his actions were he deserves forgiveness, and that many of his points still value, even if I even find him jarring and abrasive at times. I mean he's the most popular Atheist for a reason, even if sometimes he's a royal shit head.<br /> <br /> For the record I'm not an Atheist, I'm a Neo Pagan, I just enjoy his unique perpective on issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:44:39-07:00","id":989158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989106#post989106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All I know for certain is nobody is has been convicted of anything, but there is alot of mudslinging and accusations going on.<br /> <br /> And I watched the video, which I linked to, he didn't say he sexually assaults anyone. Clearly you disagree, as far as I can see people have dishonestly twisted what he said and the context in which he said them. But I doubt we'll agree on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>He does brag about sexually assaulting women, that's widely accepted by this point. He describes non-consensual sexual acts, whether it's by force or through coercion. It was even a debate question from Anderson Cooper, asking if Trump <i>understood</i> that what he said constituted sexual assault.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989106#post989106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Amazing Atheist, holy shit I had no idea he said that, and he absolutely was in the wrong, flame war or not he crossed the line. I say that as someone who writes twisted fictional porn stories in which various sexual taboos are explored), but yeah saying shit like that right to a rape victim is disgusting.<br /> <br /> But he did apologize, including to the person who he said it to and has since fundraised hundreds of thousands dollars for little girls third world to help them. So I think he's done his pence and his jack assery does nothing to change the points he made in the video. His arguements stand on its own merits.<br /> <br /> I hate trigger warning, but I'm still giving you a heads up he talks about what he wrote, which is some pretty fucked up shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/K6ys-OklTOA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do understand why you were horrified by what he said, I just believe as horrible as his actions were he deserves forgiveness, and that many of his points still value, even if I even find him jarring and abrasive at times. I mean he's the most popular Atheist for a reason, even if sometimes he's a royal shit head.<br /> <br /> For the record I'm not an Atheist, I'm a Neo Pagan, I just enjoy his unique perpective on issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm an atheist, though I've long since abandoned the internet atheist movement for being insufferably racist and sexist. I picked the most well-known example for AA, since I was already familiar with it, but it's not the only gross thing in his long catalog of misogyny and bigotry (he brags about taking upskirt shots of girls' bottoms elsewhere too, he's argued for gentrification, etc). Even excusing that stuff his reasoning in other material I've watched is usually remarkably poor, largely relying on personal anecdote in place of data. In the previous video you linked he doesn't make a single mention of Anthony Wiener, for example, because that would demolish his entire &quot;both sides are equally bad!!!&quot; argument instantly; the Democratic party of today is quick to distance itself from the kind of politician Bill Clinton was back in the 90s, comparing their behavior back then to Republican behavior <i>right now</i> says more about AA than it does modern politics. <br /> <br /> Your second video sets off too many red flags, I couldn't make it more than a minute in before I decided to end it. Seen one angry MRA mocking feminists, seen them all. It looks like from partial transcripts it doesn't get any better.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd prefer if Trump was being attacked over any of a dozen other terrible things related to his campaign and policies instead of his shitty views on women. Like the fact he's calling for his rural supporters to &quot;watch election booths&quot; in inner cities, which might be in <a href=\"https://electionlawblog.org/?p=85289\" target=\"_blank\">contravention of a Supreme Court decree</a> decree that prohibits the Republican Party from engaging in voter intimidation. Over a third of America believes that if their candidate loses an election that is proof of it being rigged, contrary to all evidence otherwise, and by golly they'll steal this election before it's stolen from them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T06:52:55-07:00","id":989326,"title":"","content":"Like I said I don't agree with AA on everything, he often takes things too far, such as the gentification bit was *face palm*.<br /> <br /> But he's often right about alot of other things, and well Diplomancy isn't his strong suit, he can be a Royal Asshole. <br /> <br /> But he still largely has an interesting perpective. He's hardcore free speech, like if he got a death threat, he'd defend their right to say it (which is too far for me, death threats aren't free speech, they're death threats).<br /> <br /> But his isn't the only perpective I listen to. I listen to The Young Turks, Shoeonhead, Tara Bacock, Sargon, Feminist Liana K, Thunderfoot, Merecedes Carrera, Honeybadgers, Feminist Camille Paglia once in a blue moon Milo, but I find I pity Milo too much to enjoy it and a host of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:22:25-07:00","id":989339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989007#post989007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If either or both candidates came out as being controlled by any of the 3 listed above, I would be more surprised that they <i>actually let that information out</i> then I would be by fact that the demons really exist or that they are in their thrall.</div> </div> </div> </div> LMFAO, in this campaign any horrible thing is possible. What a shit show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:30:54-07:00","id":989343,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the US Government is a capitalist system, and the wisdom of that system says that if I don't like a product, I should stop giving it my money and shop somewhere else.<br /> <br /> Hence why I am looking to become a citizen elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.