"count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:32:40-07:00","id":989576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989537#post989537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">USA goverment isn't capitalism at all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because a government isn't an economic system. The US government hasn't had a constant economic guiding principle. Our current system is democratic socialist safety nets and regulations on top of a capitalist corporation focused economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If everybody thinks American corporatocrations are the evil empire, but Russia and China are fogortten as potential menaces, then USA is losing the propaganda war. </div> </div> </div>Russia is definitely treated as a menace in US politics. China's potential menace is probably overly presented considering how convoluted are financial relationship has become in the past 30 years. China's relationship with the US is more complicated than &quot;enemies&quot; now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you really think the solution is the state's claws are going to save from the corporatocracies's claws? </div> </div> </div>In US law, any controls on corporations have to stem from the state. It's unavoidable in how our corporate laws are structured. Whatever words you want to use to make it sound horrible, it's not even a political philosophy issue. Going back to the Constitution, corporations have power that is solely in the control of the legislature to define, so weakening the control of corporations in politics requires using the legislature to redefine the rights corporations have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't trust anybody who try give simple explanations about politicis and economy. </div> </div> </div>Why? Being able to <b>accurately</b> explain things in simple terms is actually an incredibly potent skill. That's why Elizabeth Warren is so popular among the Democrats and the left. She really knows her economics, and she's really good at explaining them in simple terms for everyone that doesn't have advanced degrees in the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I worry about the possible electoral fraud. Trump is too much againts &quot;entablishement&quot;, and he isn't allowed to win. Electoral fraud is a serious menace for democrazy </div> </div> </div>Electoral fraud is dangerous to democracy. That's why the US makes sure it doesn't happen. More people in the US die from being struck by lightning than commit electoral fraud. Electoral fraud &quot;worries&quot; have been repeatedly proved to be nothing more than a tool Republicans are using to actually &quot;rig&quot; the election by making it harder for Democratic base voters to vote. Which is more dangerous to democracy? Less than ten people in the whole control committing fraud, or 100,000 Democratic voters being denied their vote by Republican law makers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Barack Husseim Obama's management about American army is worse than the simple blunder, it stinks of sabotage by an infiltrate, a &quot;manchurian candidate&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Citation, proof, or something? Because this is about as offensive and true as stating that the Spanish Catholic priests consider raping Muslim women appropriate penance for any sins confessed to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess the original George.R.R Martin's plan about the white walkers was like an analogy of the barbarians from the North and East of Europe who finnised off the Roman empire. </div> </div> </div>Or... they're just monsters in a fantasy setting. Not everything is a metaphor for real world events. Sometimes a pipe is just a pipe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question is... why do we say &quot;stop islamophobia&quot;, &quot;no more homophobia&quot; but not &quot;don't allow hate againts Christianity&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The question is false, because nobody actually says that Christian persecutions should be ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when I think about Hillary Clinton wants to bring those Muslim refugees to America. You are going to suffer the same fate than Europe. </div> </div> </div>Great. See me previous posts about the US refugee system and get back to me on why you feel this is a rational concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have readen in the news in Mexico some men were cut their hands like punishment for robbery. </div> </div> </div>Mexico is having a lot of trouble with organized crime, yes. It's not anarchy though, it's the fact that the US &quot;War of Drugs&quot; just made the Mexican drug cartels ruthless, well armed, and rich.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:04:09-07:00","id":989593,"title":"","content":"Regarding voter fraud, I believe that the current statistics say that out of every about 1,000,000,000 (<b>one billion</b>) votes cast since the year 2000, there have been 31<i> legitimate</i> cases of voter fraud.<br /> <br /> I think that amounts to 0.000,000,031% of actual votes being illegitimate, percentage-wise.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/