ple identifying as Muslims presages an invasion of radicals who will tear down the fundamental values of our society.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989537#post989537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I have readen in the news in Mexico some men were cut their hands like punishment for robbery. This is the true anarchy in the real world, when there isn't Law &amp; Oder, but Alan Moore didn't tell this in &quot;V of Vendetta&quot;, did he?. Anarchy isn't a group of stupy guys with Guy Fawkes' masks, but you need firearms in your home because drug-traffickers may call in your door and tell you. &quot;we like your wife, your daughrter has to go the shower because she will be the next&quot; (and this has happened in the real world. I read it in the newspaper).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alan Moore didn't present V as a saint. If you're reading it as a ringing endorsement of anarchism, you're reading it wrong. V was characterized as a radical who took extreme and questionable measures to stage a revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-18-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:24:58-07:00","id":989626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989593#post989593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding voter fraud, I believe that the current statistics say that out of every about 1,000,000,000 (<b>one billion</b>) votes cast since the year 2000, there have been 31<i> legitimate</i> cases of voter fraud.<br /> <br /> I think that amounts to 0.000,000,031% of actual votes being illegitimate, percentage-wise.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Voter fraud is too costly and risky a maneuver to work in a system as Byzantine and mechanized as the American electoral system. It can make the difference if 10 - 100 votes will shift the ballot, but for elections on the scale of a Presidential or even Congressional scale, it's of zero consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:31:15-07:00","id":989649,"title":"","content":"I will vote for Hillary Clinton in November, because <a href=\"https://medium.com/@malki/in-february-i-subscribed-to-all-the-presidential-candidates-email-lists-d9b10ca77b4d#.8nudjllqn\" target=\"_blank\">Donald Trump is a spambot</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:55:23-07:00","id":989656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989626#post989626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Voter fraud is too costly and risky a maneuver to work in a system as Byzantine and mechanized as the American electoral system. It can make the difference if 10 - 100 votes will shift the ballot, but for elections on the scale of a Presidential or even Congressional scale, it's of zero consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>To further expand on this:<br /> <br /> In the US, federal elections are still run by each state individually. And most states have different voting laws, and different organizations for their departments that run elections.<br /> <br /> To use fraud to sway the Presidential election would mean having to have a conspiracy between Democratic, Republican, and non-Partisan state run voting systems. It's simply absurd to assume any conspiracy could hold together since you would invariably have to get people of different political affiliations, all sworn to serve a non-partisan civil function, to agree to skew the system in the same direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:57:11-07:00","id":989804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989537#post989537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I <b>worry about the possible electoral fraud. Trump is too much againts &quot;entablishement&quot;, and he isn't allowed to win. Electoral fraud is a serious menace for democrazy</b>.<br /> <br /> * <b>Barack Husseim Obama's management about American army is worse than the simple blunder, it stinks of sabotage by an infiltrate, a &quot;manchurian candidate&quot;.</b><br /> * I guess the original George.R.R Martin's plan about the white walkers was like an analogy of the barbarians from the North and East of Europe who finnised off the Roman empire. I pray you understand here my point of view is different, I am not a racist, my Spanish blood may be mixture of Christians, Jews and Muslims ancestors, and I don't ashame about it. But I worry about the future of my society because for example I read days ago about a school girl who went to the hospital by a beating by her classmates. Most of the media kept quiet about the attackers were Magrehbi children. My question is... why do we say &quot;stop islamophobia&quot;, &quot;no more homophobia&quot; but not &quot;don't allow hate againts Christianity&quot;? <b>Why you can feel annoyed if anybody say anything about radical Muslims, but nothing about bad Christians?</b> I have readen this afternoon about Jude Law like the main character of a movie &quot;the young Pope&quot;. <b>Can't we tolerate xenophobia</b>, but is allowed offending Christians? Sooner or later people will start to complain about this double standar. PLEASE!!<br /> <br /> <b>And when I think about Hillary Clinton wants to bring those Muslim refugees to America. You are going to suffer the same fate than Europe.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bCan't say I didn't warn you about the offensive remarks. There are too many false statements and too much bigotry in this post to ignore. No one here defends radical Islam while attacking Christian bad actors, both are and have been subject to criticism. Your repeated attacks of other religious groups while being an apologist for Christianity's past actions is no longer tolerable. Take a week off, and if/when you come back stay out of the political discussions. You add nothing of fact or value to them and if you ignore this directive the next suspension will be permanent.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:32:11-07:00","id":990427,"title":"","content":"So I wanted to sleep on my thoughts after watching last night's debate before posting anything.<br /> <br /> Even if you're willing to dismiss repeated xenophobia, sexism, racisim and other forms of bigotry that Donald has espoused. Even if you're willing to dismiss the fact that hate groups are his most dedicated supporters. Even if you are willing to dismiss the fact that he lies constantly on things that easily fact checked 30seconds after he says them. Even if you're willing to dismiss his bad business decisions and his history of screwing other people over solely to enrich himself. Even if you're willing to dismiss his warmongering and expressed desire to see nuclear proliferation become a thing. Even if you're willing to accept all that as reasons he's unfit to be president despite him saying that he is supporting some of the policies that you want supported...<br /> <br /> He has a 30 minute attention span in a 90 minute world. The President has to spend hours and hours every day learning new things and brushing up on old things so he or she can make an educated decision that affects millions of lives (both american and non american) on a daily basis. These things aren't something that can be condensed into 5 minute briefs unless you already have done your homework on them and I don't have the confidence that Donald is able to devote that amount of time to study. Everything I've seen and read about him says that if the topic isn't about him and flattering to his ego, he starts to check out after 20-30 minutes of time <i>at most </i>and that's not something I'm comfortable in having in my president.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm<i> also </i>not willing to dismiss all that other stuff, but I believe my point stands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:47:03-07:00","id":990435,"title":"","content":"I watched the debate last night and feel better about voting for Hillary Clinton. I believe she will be a good representative of the United States to the world. Yes, she isn't a president I can sit down and have a beer with or play D&amp;D with, but frankly, I don't care about likability as much as not looking like an idiot. <br /> <br /> Also, I have quoted Jen's comment about Hillary Clinton to all of my friends and they thought it was funny. Always good to get an outside perspective. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-20-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:27:22-07:00","id":990478,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, Trump did better this last debate than the first two debates. He was less abrasive and even managed to get under Hillary's skin in their exchange about Russia (I think that's the most passion I've seen from her in this entire campaign to date).<br /> <br /> However there were a lot of issues he could have hit her with, but he just didn't bother to. When he mentioned the recent O'Keefe tapes, she didn't respond in her rebuttal and instead of hammering her, he didn't bother to bring them up again. I think he blew the debate - he's so far behind in the polls that he needed to get a KO on her and he couldn't pull that off. He also didn't press her on those comments she made about her dream for a common market with open trade and open borders, letting her get away with claiming she was only talking about it in the context of energy. She set herself up but he didn't swing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Hillary handled herself in a good, presidential manner, and artfully dodged any damaging attacks. She also managed to land some good clean hits on Trump in the process. The debate was closer than the previous two, but it was very clear that Trump completely failed in what was likely his last, best bid to attract moderates to his campaign. And without more moderates he has no chance of willing in November.<br /> <br /> Really, at this point, Trump's only hope for beating Hillary is that some horrific scandal suddenly gets revealed and is on the front page of every newspaper for the next several weeks. But at this point in the game, that seems like betting everything and then trying to draw to an inside straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-20-2016, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:12:03-07:00","id":990967,"title":"","content":"I don't know what is more depressing:<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://jezebel.com/interview-with-a-woman-who-recently-had-an-abortion-at-1781972395\" target=\"_blank\">horrific</a> <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/xojane-/this-is-what-its-really-like-to-have-a-late-term-abortion_b_8264562.html\" target=\"_blank\">stories</a> of women discussing the lengths they went to end the pain of their nonviable unborn child. <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Austin/comments/4c7fjx/my_nightmare_with_texas_womens_health_laws/\" target=\"_blank\">This story is particularly horrific.</a> <br /> <br /> Or the fact some people now believe that there are woman wantonly aborting their child at nine months. <br /> <br /> Fuck this election.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:45:43-07:00","id":990996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=990967#post990967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the fact some people now believe that there are woman wantonly aborting their child at nine months.<br /> <br /> Fuck this election.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, those people believed it before this election.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:01:02-07:00","id":991005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=990996#post990996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, those people believed it before this election.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't believe those people existed before this election. Seriously, I used to be pro-life before I read <a href=\"http://www.prochoiceactionnetwork-canada.org/articles/anti-tales.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">The Only Moral Abortion is My Abortion</a>, so I assumed I knew all the pro-life rhetoric. Apparently the message changed over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:30:47-07:00","id":991015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=991005#post991005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't believe those people existed before this election. Seriously, I used to be pro-life before I read <a href=\"http://www.prochoiceactionnetwork-canada.org/articles/anti-tales.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">The Only Moral Abortion is My Abortion</a>, so I assumed I knew all the pro-life rhetoric. Apparently the message changed over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The story that hundreds (if not thousands) of women every year get an abortion 5 minutes before they would give birth due to suddenly having cold feet about becoming a mother has, sadly, become a fairly popular story to circulate among the die-hard pro-life crowd in the last number of years. Of course it's not true, but it makes for a much more powerful image than what actually happens - and by making it appear that these kind of &quot;last minute&quot; abortions (which in fact pretty much never happen) are the most common type of abortion, the pro-life crowd can get more people on board with their message.<br /> <br /> For many in the pro-life community with the awareness of what actually happens, they don't see any moral issue with greatly exaggerating (or just flat out flying) about what happens during abortions - their goal is to save lives, and in their opinion, making up a few tall tales or exaggerating the facts is a small sin to weigh against a half-million lives every year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:17:55-07:00","id":991059,"title":"","content":"There are pro-life murder apologists that defend people that have killed people for providing abortions.<br /> <br /> I really wish this election was some sort of eye-opening moment about the worst of the worst in the pro-life radicals, but it really isn't. Most Republicans know better than to say those things on the debate stage, but they've been saying it in the primaries for decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:23:26-07:00","id":991166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=991059#post991059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are pro-life murder apologists that defend people that have killed people for providing abortions.<br /> <br /> I really wish this election was some sort of eye-opening moment about the worst of the worst in the pro-life radicals, but it really isn't. Most Republicans know better than to say those things on the debate stage, but they've been saying it in the primaries for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS eye-opening, but not in the inward-focused soul-searching kind of way.<br /> <br /> It's eye-opening in the &quot;I never really knew who my neighbors were&quot; kind of way, if you're only just now realizing how much you disagree with people in the opposing party.<br /> <br /> It's eye-opening in the &quot;I am now learning what it means to be a minority in my own country,&quot; kind of way, if you're about to lose an election and realizing that your ideology has effectively disenfranchised you.<br /> <br /> It's eye-opening in the &quot;Some parts of our laws enable extremism to thrive,&quot; kind of way, if you're an academic who was completely blindsided by the rise of Trump.<br /> <br /> And it's eye-opening in the &quot;We have to collectively become better people someway, somehow,&quot; kind of way, if you are only just now realizing how much we have to overcome before we can really start living up to our national ideals. If you're in this last group, you're probably going to spend the rest of your life fighting with others about what it means to be &quot;better&quot; and how to achieve that state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T18:15:04-07:00","id":991198,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's a location difference. But I know of a multiple billboards (like big signs on the side of major roads) that have been taken out by pro-life organizations for at least 10 years. Some are reasonably tame emotional pleas to guilt pregnant mothers over the life inside of them. Others are vile and toe the line of advocating violence against those that provide abortion. I regularly see similar nasty things on bumper stickers as well. I see this shit all the time. Hearing Trump say it in the final debate was to me someone saying what I've heard lots of his base say.<br /> <br /> But if you follow the fight to keep abortion legal, this is nothing new.<br /> <br /> I already knew these people were my neighbors. I was already acutely aware of how disenfranchised many of them feel as the people they vote for can't stop the changing cultural landscape of the country. I'm was already painfully aware of how are laws enable extremism to thrive.<br /> <br /> None of this was a shock to me twenty years ago when I first had to confront such forces in the society around me. So Trump doesn't shock me on these things now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:25:30-07:00","id":991776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=991005#post991005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't believe those people existed before this election. Seriously, I used to be pro-life before I read <a href=\"http://www.prochoiceactionnetwork-canada.org/articles/anti-tales.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">The Only Moral Abortion is My Abortion</a>, so I assumed I knew all the pro-life rhetoric. Apparently the message changed over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never read any Pro-Life rhetoric that refers to themselves as &quot;Anti-Choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> <s>Be sort of like referring to ones self as &quot;Pro-Infanticide.&quot;</s><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":".  Reeked of uncivil accusations about a touchy subject, I apologize. 10-23-2016, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T03:10:29-07:00","id":991789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989410#post989410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYou ever get the feeling that Dems and Republicans are respectively Target and Walmart, and the Independent candidates are the mom and pop stores that get pushed out of business because they can't compete with the scale of the big two retailers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Course it's not like the third party candidates are selling anything I want to throw a vote at.<br /> Green Party's an Anti-Vaxxer. Libertarian's is Pro Gun Control. Communists' is a frigging communist. I'd sooner vote for a Circus Clown than any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:09:28-07:00","id":992367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=990478#post990478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, Trump did better this last debate than the first two debates. He was less abrasive and even managed to get under Hillary's skin in their exchange about Russia (I think that's the most passion I've seen from her in this entire campaign to date).<br /> <br /> However there were a lot of issues he could have hit her with, but he just didn't bother to. When he mentioned the recent O'Keefe tapes, she didn't respond in her rebuttal and instead of hammering her, he didn't bother to bring them up again. I think he blew the debate - he's so far behind in the polls that he needed to get a KO on her and he couldn't pull that off. He also didn't press her on those comments she made about her dream for a common market with open trade and open borders, letting her get away with claiming she was only talking about it in the context of energy. She set herself up but he didn't swing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Hillary handled herself in a good, presidential manner, and artfully dodged any damaging attacks. She also managed to land some good clean hits on Trump in the process. The debate was closer than the previous two, but it was very clear that Trump completely failed in what was likely his last, best bid to attract moderates to his campaign. And without more moderates he has no chance of willing in November.<br /> <br /> Really, at this point, Trump's only hope for beating Hillary is that some horrific scandal suddenly gets revealed and is on the front page of every newspaper for the next several weeks. But at this point in the game, that seems like betting everything and then trying to draw to an inside straight.</div> </div> </div> </div> If said scandal happened, you'd find a dozen new rape or sexual assualt or sexual harrassment accusations aginst Trump magically appear out of the wood work, and the media focusing on that while ignoring Hillary's scandals.<br /> <br /> I've decided to withdraw my endorsement of Hillary, she's playing a level dirty pool that I can't support and it appears she's backing away from the progressive promises she made during the race with Bernie Sanders.<br /> <br /> So I officially endorse metorite 2016, because it seems like the most humane solution to this crapastic election.<br /> <br /> Write in you ballots for the metorite, for favourite celebrities or porn stars, write in your childerns names, it doesn't matter matter as long as the people running things gets the point, FUCK YOU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:15:10-07:00","id":992410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=992367#post992367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If said scandal happened, you'd find a dozen new rape or sexual assualt or sexual harrassment accusations aginst Trump magically appear out of the wood work, and the media focusing on that while ignoring Hillary's scandals.<br /> <br /> I've decided to withdraw my endorsement of Hillary, she's playing a level dirty pool that I can't support and it appears she's backing away from the progressive promises she made during the race with Bernie Sanders.<br /> <br /> So I officially endorse metorite 2016, because it seems like the most humane solution to this crapastic election.<br /> <br /> Write in you ballots for the metorite, for favourite celebrities or porn stars, write in your childerns names, it doesn't matter matter as long as the people running things gets the point, FUCK YOU.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem is they won't. It would take a very mobilized and pointed act of contempt to get any attention from the party candidates, and at that point, you're better off mobilizing behind a third party candidate. At least then the party liners will have <i>some</i> idea what the discontent want them to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:26:49-07:00","id":992527,"title":"","content":"One of the big reasons why write-in &quot;protest&quot; votes don't actually work?<br /> <br /> 43 states don't even have to record them. A small number of states don't even allow write-ins at all, and the majority of states require a write-in candidate to still have registered with the state in some fashion for any votes for them to count.<br /> <br /> While people like to push the &quot;throwing your vote away&quot; around third party candidates, at least with a major third party there are non-winning voting milestones they can aim to hit. Voting a &quot;protest&quot; write-in is literally throwing your vote away for most Americans because it'll be recorded the same as if you abstained.<br /> <br /> The rules are purposefully designed so that the people running things can completely ignore the &quot;point&quot; of trying to give them the finger with a protest vote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:22:57-07:00","id":992547,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu 2016: Why settle for the lesser evil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:46:38-07:00","id":992551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zeroninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=992547#post992547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthulhu 2016: Why settle for the lesser evil?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat will literally be on the T-shirt I wear to the polls on election day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T13:56:11-07:00","id":992556,"title":"","content":"Sad that that's been applicable since 1998.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/3e/57/31/3e5731d112d97ad45412a9967330a9ba.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:09:47-07:00","id":992563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=992527#post992527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the big reasons why write-in &quot;protest&quot; votes don't actually work?<br /> <br /> 43 states don't even have to record them. A small number of states don't even allow write-ins at all, and the majority of states require a write-in candidate to still have registered with the state in some fashion for any votes for them to count.<br /> <br /> While people like to push the &quot;throwing your vote away&quot; around third party candidates, at least with a major third party there are non-winning voting milestones they can aim to hit. Voting a &quot;protest&quot; write-in is literally throwing your vote away for most Americans because it'll be recorded the same as if you abstained.<br /> <br /> The rules are purposefully designed so that the people running things can completely ignore the &quot;point&quot; of trying to give them the finger with a protest vote.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And Gary Johnson is poised to take 5% of the vote, which is the bar for getting federal funding. I don't really like libertarianism, but that's a good sign for pushing against the two party system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:55:15-07:00","id":992631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=992551#post992551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat will literally be on the T-shirt I wear to the polls on election day.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.cafepress.com/+cthulhu-2016+t-shirts\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cafepress.com/+cthulhu-2016+t-shirts</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T18:03:00-07:00","id":993812,"title":"","content":"I think that one would be be a problem since it advocates for a particular candidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T15:43:22-07:00","id":994248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=992563#post992563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And Gary Johnson is poised to take 5% of the vote, which is the bar for getting federal funding. I don't really like libertarianism, but that's a good sign for pushing against the two party system.</div> </div> </div> </div> What kind of funding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:25:43-07:00","id":994270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994248#post994248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of funding?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you file your taxes, you have the option to make a donation to the Presidential Election Campaign Fund. That basically serves as a grant for candidates. That money is apportioned out to all parties that qualify (and a 5% voter share in the last election is a requirement). A quick glance online showed that the RNC and DNC both got about $19,000,000 in funding from the PECF. I'm not sure if it's awarded proportionally or somehow adjusted according to need or priority, but that's almost double the amount of money Johnson's raised in this election cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:47:09-07:00","id":994322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994270#post994270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you file your taxes, you have the option to make a donation to the Presidential Election Campaign Fund. That basically serves as a grant for candidates. That money is apportioned out to all parties that qualify (and a 5% voter share in the last election is a requirement). A quick glance online showed that the RNC and DNC both got about $19,000,000 in funding from the PECF. I'm not sure if it's awarded proportionally or somehow adjusted according to need or priority, but that's almost double the amount of money Johnson's raised in this election cycle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, cool, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T19:15:34-07:00","id":994339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pADHLsECWxY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pADHLsECWxY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/pADHLsECWxY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/pADHLsECWxY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> According to Michael Moore Trump's election to President is going to be American biggest fuck you to the elites.<br /> <br /> I never thought Michael Moore would say anything like this. Calls Trump the malotov cocktail, the hand grenade the public plans to throw.<br /> <br /> Point out that Trump went to the board of Ford and said right to their face, if you keep sending American jobs to Mexico, I'll hit you with a 35% tarriff that will make sure no buys it. Fucking ballsy. I wish Prime Minister Justin Trudeau would do that instead being Captain Selfie and reneging on promises. I do feel bad for Mexico if Trump wins.<br /> <br /> Moore also points out that alot of Trump supporters are racists or anything, its just people fed up with losing time and again, people and communities who have lost everything to corporist trade agreements that promised more jobs and wealth and delivered neither to ordinary people.<br /> <br /> I disagree with say most of Trumps policies, roughly 95%, except trade policies where as big a goof as he is, he's absolutely right that the common folks got fucked on these deals. You want to know what the last treaty to actually create jobs was?<br /> <br /> The Auto Pact between Canada and America, that created manufacturing jobs for both countries.<br /> <br /> Honestly after the tape was leaked, I honestly thought Trump was fucked, that there was no way he was coming back from that, double digit drop, but if a progressive champion like Micheal Moore can make such a point in Trumps favour, basically if you having nothing left, but your vote, then there is no reason not to vote Trump and let it all fucking burn, then Trump might still have a chance.<br /> <br /> Either way he's going to leave the GOP in fucking ashes, so I can celebrate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:02:29-07:00","id":994357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994339#post994339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point out that Trump went to the board of Ford and said right to their face, if you keep sending American jobs to Mexico, I'll hit you with a 35% tarriff that will make sure no buys it. Fucking ballsy. I wish Prime Minister Justin Trudeau would do that instead being Captain Selfie and reneging on promises. I do feel bad for Mexico if Trump wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ballsy yes. Making threats of illegal actions that trash the economy of the country are very much in that range.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994339#post994339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moore also points out that alot of Trump supporters are racists or anything, its just people fed up with losing time and again, people and communities who have lost everything to corporist trade agreements that promised more jobs and wealth and delivered neither to ordinary people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, that is fully understandable. Believing the promises of politicians and corporate representatives when they shake hands and say 'this will bring many jobs' or 'this is a really good thing' is never a good idea. They sell ideas that sound good, not ideas that employ people.<br /> <br /> America already had a lovely go-around with the protectionist trade practices of jacking up import taxes on products that compete with american goods and production... it results in all those other countries slapping import taxes on american goods, causing the economy to slow down and american companies being devalued. The reason the jobs that used to be heavy in the rustbelt and elsewhere went overseas wasn't a lack of taxes being slapped on stuff coming into the country, it's the very simple fact that with modern infrastructure, modern shipping, and modern organizational technologies it is considerably cheaper to employ people elsewhere in the world and ship the goods to the US and across the US than it is to make them there.<br /> <br /> China is the example of the reverse in action. Dropping trade barriers and taxes, suddenly an influx of outside goods, localization of the products, and they become a powerhouse selling to both the domestic and global market.<br /> <br /> Slapping taxes that the US has agreed internationally NOT to apply (under threat of large taxes being slapped on them) will not help. At best it would drive down demand for the products of that company as the prices get jacked up. Which just means they move their offices out of the non-profitable US and relocate elsewhere. Meanwhile the worst is that it establishes the US as a nation even less likely to honor the treaties it signs. Which means nobody trusts it. If you want to see a country collapse in a hurry, make it so the international banks don't want to business with that government because they're not considered as trustworthy anymore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:41:32-07:00","id":994376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994357#post994357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ballsy yes. Making threats of illegal actions that trash the economy of the country are very much in that range.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well yes, that is fully understandable. Believing the promises of politicians and corporate representatives when they shake hands and say 'this will bring many jobs' or 'this is a really good thing' is never a good idea. They sell ideas that sound good, not ideas that employ people.<br /> <br /> America already had a lovely go-around with the protectionist trade practices of jacking up import taxes on products that compete with american goods and production... it results in all those other countries slapping import taxes on american goods, causing the economy to slow down and american companies being devalued. The reason the jobs that used to be heavy in the rustbelt and elsewhere went overseas wasn't a lack of taxes being slapped on stuff coming into the country, it's the very simple fact that with modern infrastructure, modern shipping, and modern organizational technologies it is considerably cheaper to employ people elsewhere in the world and ship the goods to the US and across the US than it is to make them there.<br /> <br /> China is the example of the reverse in action. Dropping trade barriers and taxes, suddenly an influx of outside goods, localization of the products, and they become a powerhouse selling to both the domestic and global market.<br /> <br /> Slapping taxes that the US has agreed internationally NOT to apply (under threat of large taxes being slapped on them) will not help. At best it would drive down demand for the products of that company as the prices get jacked up. Which just means they move their offices out of the non-profitable US and relocate elsewhere. Meanwhile the worst is that it establishes the US as a nation even less likely to honor the treaties it signs. Which means nobody trusts it. If you want to see a country collapse in a hurry, make it so the international banks don't want to business with that government because they're not considered as trustworthy anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. There's this oversimplified conversation about how neoliberal Democrats are pushing globalization and populist Republicans are trying to stop it. That's not how it works. Globalization isn't an agenda. It's an inevitability spurred by dramatic technological shifts and the growth of smaller nations out of colonialism. Its not about pushing globalization or halting it. It's about recognizing it as an unstoppable shift in global policy and altering your policy to match that. Those jobs aren't just going to come back when there are other nations better equipped to fill them, and punishing businesses for taking advantages of these opportunities will just further cripple our economy. What we need is to adjust our economy to stay at the forefront of the tech revolution, to be the pioneer in new industries, but our woefully inadequate education system, stymied political structure, and parasitic corporatism makes us ill-equipped to train our people and promote those kinds of jobs. It's a complicated issue that neither party (and no one person, really) has the answers to. I can't blame people for being angry. I can understand why they latch on to a demagogue. But that doesn't make that attachment any less toxic for our country.<br /> <br /> You can recognize that someone is justified being angry and too uneducated to understand the implications of why they're angry, and you can still recognize how disastrous that ignorance is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:39:24-07:00","id":994436,"title":"","content":"Also, let's remember the quoting people out of context rarely ends well. Michael Moore's point is actually an indictment of Trump. Yes, he's saying how a lot of people feel, and why those feelings are driving them towards Trump, but the ultimate goal of <u>Michael Moore in Trumpland</u> is not &quot;Sure vote for Trump and blow it all up!&quot; but rather, &quot;No, I really do get you folks, you're not wrong about all these things you're angry about, you should be angry about them, but throwing that hand grenade isn't going to solve your problems.... so lets talk about what actually would (hint: vote Clinton now, and Sanders-types later).&quot;<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Also, Trump can threaten whatever he wants. It's one of his default modes (see the recent list of all the people he's threatened to sue) to dealing with stuff he doesn't like. But just like those law suits, his threats to Ford are nonsense and everyone at Ford knows it. Why? Because the President doesn't have that power. Trump has no plan to actually deal with things like the Congress and statutory limitations on Presidential powers the judiciary will enforce. If he gets elected he's probably relying on those to blame for why all his promises aren't going to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:09:13-07:00","id":994489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994436#post994436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, let's remember the quoting people out of context rarely ends well. Michael Moore's point is actually an indictment of Trump. Yes, he's saying how a lot of people feel, and why those feelings are driving them towards Trump, but the ultimate goal of <u>Michael Moore in Trumpland</u> is not &amp;quot;Sure vote for Trump and blow it all up!&amp;quot; but rather, &amp;quot;No, I really do get you folks, you're not wrong about all these things you're angry about, you should be angry about them, but throwing that hand grenade isn't going to solve your problems.... so lets talk about what actually would (hint: vote Clinton now, and Sanders-types later).&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Also, Trump can threaten whatever he wants. It's one of his default modes (see the recent list of all the people he's threatened to sue) to dealing with stuff he doesn't like. But just like those law suits, his threats to Ford are nonsense and everyone at Ford knows it. Why? Because the President doesn't have that power. Trump has no plan to actually deal with things like the Congress and statutory limitations on Presidential powers the judiciary will enforce. If he gets elected he's probably relying on those to blame for why all his promises aren't going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very possible. Look I'm not saying Mike a Trump fan, I just find it interesting, that things have gotten to this point, and that it might still be possible for Trump to win.<br /> <br /> Look I withdrew my endorsement of Hillary, but I sure don't endorse Trump either. Its your election, not mine, its you pile of crap to clean up, not mine. As a Canadian we have our own problems with Prime Minister Selfie and Prime Minister Darth Vadar before him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:04:17-07:00","id":994647,"title":"","content":"You know it's a strange election when Texas is polling as a swing state and Michael Moore is expressing sympathy for supporters of the Republican candidate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-28-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:19:55-07:00","id":994654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994647#post994647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know it's a strange election when Texas is polling as a swing state and Michael Moore is expressing sympathy for supporters of the Republican candidate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't these listed as signs of the apocalypse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:44:25-07:00","id":994665,"title":"","content":"First two seals, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:02:21-07:00","id":994693,"title":"","content":"If my life has taught me anything about Texas, when they heard where the Republican candidate was from, they all exclaimed, '<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mSxnieYctVM\" target=\"_blank\">New York City!</a>'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:11:52-07:00","id":994702,"title":"","content":"Everything constructive I had to say has been said. So I'm putting a video that amused me in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kbryz0mxuMY\" data-code=\"Kbryz0mxuMY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Kbryz0mxuMY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:16:49-07:00","id":994740,"title":"","content":"Just saw on TV Hillary Clinton taking about Trump appearence on Howard Stern.<br /> <br /> That Howard Stern in featuring in presidential nominee speeches at all could be the next seal.<br /> <br /> I know I started laughing at the Surrealism of it all. This is a the future of politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:34:23-07:00","id":994754,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2016/10/howard-stern-donald-trump-2016-214322\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.politico.com/magazine/sto...mp-2016-214322</a><br /> <br /> Man, Trump must hate Howard Stern now. I still can't believe Howard Stern is so important to the American election. Just surreal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:48:02-07:00","id":994760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=987449#post987449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actions speak louder than words and Trump has shown what sort of person he prefers to have stand at his side. While Trump might not personally have any issues with the LBGTQRS community, he has shown that he is perfectly willing to support and assist people who want to strip the members of the that community's rights away from them. And I can't support someone who is willing to stand shoulder to shoulder with bigots who would deny gays and others their constitutionally God-given rights simply in the name of political expediency.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, Y'know that Clinton has John Mccain in her camp right along with the rest of the old folks from the Republican party who don't WANT a new face for it? And also actually was against Gay rights until it was no longer politically expedient? And blatantly referred to African American youth as Super-predators and described them as sociopathic killing machines?<br /> <br /> That's the only guarantee you have with Clinton. She's on your side until you're no longer politically expedient. Right now, Trump has solidly wrapped certain demographics around his finger, so she went for the others. Because political expediency is all she cares about. Anything to get her power and money.<br /> <br /> Anyway, they're all terrible, don't lie to yourself and convince yourself Clinton is any better than Trump is. Vote what you honestly think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:38:42-07:00","id":994790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994754#post994754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, Trump must hate Howard Stern now. I still can't believe Howard Stern is so important to the American election. Just surreal.</div> </div> </div> </div>He probably does, but it's not as if Stern was planning to ruin his 2016 presidential hopes. Everything Trump said was just Trump being himself. I don't know if Stern actually put out those recordings, the article doesn't suggest he came forward with them. People have been listening to him for so long and knew Trump was a common guest and being a presidential candidate now would be the time to bring it up.<br /> <br /> Got my early voting done, I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:51:40-07:00","id":994913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994760#post994760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Y'know that Clinton has John Mccain in her camp right along with the rest of the old folks from the Republican party who don't WANT a new face for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what exactly? Mccain's whole campaign right now is, &quot;Trump can't win, so you have to vote for me to make sure the Senate stays Republican to make sure Hillary can't do anything in office.&quot; That's not exactly &quot;being in the Clinton camp,&quot; as much as, &quot;Trump is a loser and I don't want to go down with him.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And also actually was against Gay rights until it was no longer politically expedient? </div> </div> </div>Not true. One of the things people forget about progress... is that the past was worse. A lot of what the Clintons said in the 90s about gay rights seem horrible now, but were progressive then. &quot;Don't ask, Don't tell,&quot; was meant to help gays in the military, not hurt them, by allowing them to stay in the closet and not get punished for lying about it.<br /> <br /> Now, we've all moved past that, and think of such a policy as ridiculous, but that fails to recognize that the first laws on the progress towards civil rights have always been messy stumbling blocks that are the first steps towards breaking the mold that eventually gets us to better laws. Without the Clintons being in the push to say that gays in the military should actually be allowed at all, we'd probably be far less along the path towards full LGBTQ civil rights.<br /> <br /> And there's also the issue of turning such things into a Catch-22 for politicians. If &quot;evolving&quot; on an issue is a bad thing... what exactly is a politician supposed to do? Should Clinton revert to outdated and bigoted LGBTQ policies that she says she doesn't believe in anymore so she can avoid looking like she's changing for political expediency, or change her position according to whatever thoughts convinced her to change and look like she's been an opportunist?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, Lincoln was super racist by today's standards, but goes down in history for his role in black civil rights because he picked a political position that was the right direction for progress.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And blatantly referred to African American youth as Super-predators and described them as sociopathic killing machines? </div> </div> </div>Well... no. She referred to gangs grooming youth to be superpredators as something that had to be stopped. It's a reasonable inference from the rest of her speech that she was talking about youths of color, because she was talking about violent crime in the African American community previously in the speech, and it's very hard to separate the intersection of inner-city gang activity, urban poverty, and the socio-economic struggles of communities of color in this country. <br /> <br /> So she never directly called African American youth superpredators, and it was never a blanket statement about all of them. Of course, it was still a horrible thing to say... which is why she's said so in hindsight. But again, go back to the Catch-22 problem if we never allow politicians to correct themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the only guarantee you have with Clinton. She's on your side until you're no longer politically expedient. </div> </div> </div>So, her whole failed health care push as First Lady that was completely not politically expedient doesn't count? Her record is full of things that don't follow this mindset.<br /> <br /> Now, you can fairly say her record indicates she has causes she really cares about and will damn the political expediency, and others she's less committed to and thus is more likely to make significant compromises on... but who is that not true for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, they're all terrible, don't lie to yourself and convince yourself Clinton is any better than Trump is. Vote what you honestly think. </div> </div> </div>I don't need to lie to myself. I can be convinced that Clinton way, way, way better than Trump is based on nice solid facts, and then vote honestly on just that. And then be smug about voting for people that actually fight for voting rights (even if just for political expediency, because I don't care if it's just for political expediency if it's for what I believe is the right cause; I don't need the whole world to be made of true believers to believe the system can work) that protect people's right to vote for whatever reasons they decide to, instead of voting for more power to the political party that has no issue using voter suppression to make sure they stay in power (and probably will have no issue doing things to reduce the amount of power in their own districts to help avoid another Trump).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:51:12-07:00","id":994979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994489#post994489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very possible. Look I'm not saying Mike a Trump fan, I just find it interesting, that things have gotten to this point, and that it might still be possible for Trump to win.<br /> <br /> Look I withdrew my endorsement of Hillary, but I sure don't endorse Trump either. Its your election, not mine, its you pile of crap to clean up, not mine. As a Canadian we have our own problems with Prime Minister Selfie and Prime Minister Darth Vadar before him.</div> </div> </div> </div>... you're Canadian too? Is this thread just a bunch of us arguing over US politics?<br /> <br /> Irregardless, anyone following US politics closely is aware by now that it's become impossible for Trump to win the election. Clinton's margins are too high in states adding up to 272 electoral votes (on Oct 26th: VA +8.8, NH +8.1, MN +8.0, MI +7.6, WI +7.2, CO +7.1, PA +7.1). Mainstream media obsessed with the &quot;horserace&quot; are forced to cover states like FL or NC just to get something remotely resembling a close contest in polling/early voting and even there they miss what's actually happening. The narrative of &quot;things are close!&quot; is too important to get eyeballs watching TV. Meanwhile good journalism has moved on to following the real stories at the moment in the Senate/House races that are still unpredictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","user":"Shinjo","date":". 10-28-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T18:36:03-07:00","id":994990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994647#post994647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know it's a strange election when Texas is polling as a swing state and Michael Moore is expressing sympathy for supporters of the Republican candidate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never thought, in a million years I'd feel empathize, politically with Glenn Beck.<br /> There was a part of me that feels like I should be enjoying this. But I'm not. I can't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:29:30-07:00","id":995014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994665#post994665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First two seals, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CtNDVs8Y4cI\" target=\"_blank\">Not true seals, though.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:08:23-07:00","id":995036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994979#post994979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... you're Canadian too? Is this thread just a bunch of us arguing over US politics?<br /> <br /> Irregardless, anyone following US politics closely is aware by now that it's become impossible for Trump to win the election. Clinton's margins are too high in states adding up to 272 electoral votes (on Oct 26th: VA +8.8, NH +8.1, MN +8.0, MI +7.6, WI +7.2, CO +7.1, PA +7.1). Mainstream media obsessed with the &amp;quot;horserace&amp;quot; are forced to cover states like FL or NC just to get something remotely resembling a close contest in polling/early voting and even there they miss what's actually happening. The narrative of &amp;quot;things are close!&amp;quot; is too important to get eyeballs watching TV. Meanwhile good journalism has moved on to following the real stories at the moment in the Senate/House races that are still unpredictable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I'm a follow Canadian.<br /> <br /> And I'm to the point where I don't even give a fuck who wins. Hillary has another email scandal out. If she wins, the Senate and Congress need to keep her the fuck away from the internet.<br /> <br /> Its like watching a car accident, I can't look away anymore.<br /> <br /> As for the polls, I'm hearing from people that they're full of shit and honestly it wouldn't be the first time, they're right sometimes, bit other times they blow chunks. So I don't know.<br /> <br /> Right now I think America should just let Canada invade and make it the 11th province.<br /> <br /> You know what the next time the Americans give you a hard time about the Canadian Monarchy, you remind them about this election.<br /> <br /> Say what you will about the Queen, at least she never called Mexicans rapists and tried to build a wall to keep them out and at least she knows enough to keep private emails private and not to conspire with Guardian &quot;journalists&quot; to smear Bernie Sanders falsely as a mysgonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:17:17-07:00","id":995042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994760#post994760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, they're all terrible, don't lie to yourself and convince yourself Clinton is any better than Trump is. Vote what you honestly think.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the end of the day, Hillary is a career politician. If she becomes president, we know exactly what we're getting - a continuation of Obama's policies and an attempt to return America to where it was in the mid-90's under her husband (and let's be honest, American in the mid-90s wasn't exactly the worst period of time in the history of America).<br /> <br /> With Trump, though, who knows what he will do if he wins. Hell, who knows what he will do if he <i>loses</i> - he's the first major presidential candidate in the history of the United States to suggest he might refuse to accept the results of the election. With the exception of the Wall on the southern border, he has changed his stance on nearly every other issue - first he's for a blanket ban on Muslims, then he's not. Then he's for using force on Syria, then he's not. He was pro-life before running, now he's completely anti-abortion.<br /> <br /> I can safely say that while I personally detest Hillary, she won't be the worst president we've ever had, we know what she'll want to do and we know the Republicans will use every footdragging technique in their power to prevent her from doing anything at all. Absolute worst case scenario, we have 4 years of political deadlock and 4 years with only eight people on the Supreme Court because the Republicans refuse to hold hearings on anyone that Clinton nominates. But, hey, we had 4 years of deadlock under Clinton's second term and 4 years of deadlock under Obama's second term.<br /> <br /> But I can't safely say anything about Trump other than the fact that electing him is rolling some dice. Maybe he'd be good, I mean I guess it's theoretically possible? But more than likely, Trump's obvious lack of self-control would be pretty bad for the country - at the least, someone who has exhibited as little control over themselves as Trump has throughout this election cycle isn't going to do a great job.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I just don't feel comfortable gambling on the long odds like that with the future of America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-28-2016, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T06:36:41-07:00","id":995171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994979#post994979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anyone following US politics closely is aware by now that it's become impossible for Trump to win the election.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Statistician, I feel I must inform you that the odds of Trump winning are currently estimated at 9% by <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/upshot/presidential-polls-forecast.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2...-forecast.html</a>, which sounds small until you remember it's darned close to one in ten. So in one of eleven possible futures, President Trump is elected next Tuesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:59:42-07:00","id":995196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995171#post995171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Statistician, I feel I must inform you that the odds of Trump winning are currently estimated at 9% by <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/upshot/presidential-polls-forecast.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2...-forecast.html</a>, which sounds small until you remember it's darned close to one in ten. So in one of eleven possible futures, President Trump is elected next Tuesday.</div> </div> </div> </div>And FiveThirtyEight has the odds just under 20%. Any election is going to come with factors we can't predict, and that's especially true in this election (particularly given the abnormally large number of independent and undecided voters less than two weeks from voting day).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:02:40-07:00","id":995198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994760#post994760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, Y'know that Clinton has John Mccain in her camp right along with the rest of the old folks from the Republican party who don't WANT a new face for it? And also actually was against Gay rights until it was no longer politically expedient? And blatantly referred to African American youth as Super-predators and described them as sociopathic killing machines?<br /> <br /> That's the only guarantee you have with Clinton. She's on your side until you're no longer politically expedient. Right now, Trump has solidly wrapped certain demographics around his finger, so she went for the others. Because political expediency is all she cares about. Anything to get her power and money.<br /> <br /> Anyway, they're all terrible, don't lie to yourself and convince yourself Clinton is any better than Trump is. Vote what you honestly think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Better a competent pragmatist than a grossly inadequate egotist.<br /> <br /> I might not like her as a person, but there's no doubt she's a savvy politician; and I'd rather gain two yards than have a QB hurl the ball at the bleachers and then call it a whore. I don't give a shit <i>why</i> she pushes the policy she does. All I care is that it gets pushed.<br /> <br /> And if the face of the &quot;New Republican Party&quot; is thinly veiled racist and xenophobic fucks masquerading as populists, I'm happy to keep the old guard relevant. At least they have some decorum with their hate speech. At least when an old school Republican gives me some brokeass talk about the Voter Rights Act, I can trust he's driven more by political strategy than racist zealotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-29-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:15:58-07:00","id":995205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=994913#post994913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on what exactly? Mccain's whole campaign right now is, &quot;Trump can't win, so you have to vote for me to make sure the Senate stays Republican to make sure Hillary can't do anything in office.&quot; That's not exactly &quot;being in the Clinton camp,&quot; as much as, &quot;Trump is a loser and I don't want to go down with him.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not true. One of the things people forget about progress... is that the past was worse. A lot of what the Clintons said in the 90s about gay rights seem horrible now, but were progressive then. &quot;Don't ask, Don't tell,&quot; was meant to help gays in the military, not hurt them, by allowing them to stay in the closet and not get punished for lying about it.<br /> <br /> Now, we've all moved past that, and think of such a policy as ridiculous, but that fails to recognize that the first laws on the progress towards civil rights have always been messy stumbling blocks that are the first steps towards breaking the mold that eventually gets us to better laws. Without the Clintons being in the push to say that gays in the military should actually be allowed at all, we'd probably be far less along the path towards full LGBTQ civil rights.<br /> <br /> And there's also the issue of turning such things into a Catch-22 for politicians. If &quot;evolving&quot; on an issue is a bad thing... what exactly is a politician supposed to do? Should Clinton revert to outdated and bigoted LGBTQ policies that she says she doesn't believe in anymore so she can avoid looking like she's changing for political expediency, or change her position according to whatever thoughts convinced her to change and look like she's been an opportunist?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, Lincoln was super racist by today's standards, but goes down in history for his role in black civil rights because he picked a political position that was the right direction for progress.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well... no. She referred to gangs grooming youth to be superpredators as something that had to be stopped. It's a reasonable inference from the rest of her speech that she was talking about youths of color, because she was talking about violent crime in the African American community previously in the speech, and it's very hard to separate the intersection of inner-city gang activity, urban poverty, and the socio-economic struggles of communities of color in this country.<br /> <br /> So she never directly called African American youth superpredators, and it was never a blanket statement about all of them. Of course, it was still a horrible thing to say... which is why she's said so in hindsight. But again, go back to the Catch-22 problem if we never allow politicians to correct themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, her whole failed health care push as First Lady that was completely not politically expedient doesn't count? Her record is full of things that don't follow this mindset.<br /> <br /> Now, you can fairly say her record indicates she has causes she really cares about and will damn the political expediency, and others she's less committed to and thus is more likely to make significant compromises on... but who is that not true for?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't need to lie to myself. I can be convinced that Clinton way, way, way better than Trump is based on nice solid facts, and then vote honestly on just that. And then be smug about voting for people that actually fight for voting rights (even if just for political expediency, because I don't care if it's just for political expediency if it's for what I believe is the right cause; I don't need the whole world to be made of true believers to believe the system can work) that protect people's right to vote for whatever reasons they decide to, instead of voting for more power to the political party that has no issue using voter suppression to make sure they stay in power (and probably will have no issue doing things to reduce the amount of power in their own districts to help avoid another Trump).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^ Real talk. You've quickly become one of my favorite posters in this forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">... you're Canadian too? Is this thread just a bunch of us arguing over US politics?<br /> <br /> Irregardless, anyone following US politics closely is aware by now that it's become impossible for Trump to win the election. Clinton's margins are too high in states adding up to 272 electoral votes (on Oct 26th: VA +8.8, NH +8.1, MN +8.0, MI +7.6, WI +7.2, CO +7.1, PA +7.1). Mainstream media obsessed with the &quot;horserace&quot; are forced to cover states like FL or NC just to get something remotely resembling a close contest in polling/early voting and even there they miss what's actually happening. The narrative of &quot;things are close!&quot; is too important to get eyeballs watching TV. Meanwhile good journalism has moved on to following the real stories at the moment in the Senate/House races that are still unpredictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll agree that the Senate and House races are more important by a long shot, but that doesn't mean the presidential race isn't important. Trump's chances of winning are a long shot, but it's still a shot, and people beat worse odds every day. He's only 5-6 points behind Clinton, which is pretty goddamn worrying for us as a nation. And Clinton winning is important, but Clinton winning <i>definitively </i>is even more important. It determines how she's viewed by the public and how the RNC and DNC accordingly respond. It determines how much push she has against her policy, and it could have a major effect on how and how quickly the Republican Party crumbles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:19:03-07:00","id":995234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995036#post995036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now I think America should just let Canada invade and make it the 11th province.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, don't even joke. Whoever's elected, if they do a bad job they'll be out in four years. If they did a good job they'd be out in 8. If we wanted to surrender ourselves to a foreign government we would have gotten rid of the second amendment long ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know what the next time the Americans give you a hard time about the Canadian Monarchy, you remind them about this election. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's a thing outside of the Simpsons and the show with Cobie Smulders. Around this time eight years ago people were swearing up and down that if Barack Hussein Obama, they had to put in his middle name because it links him with Saddam Hussein, was elected, he would change the name of the White House to the Black House, and the pledge allegiance to state that we were, 'One nation, under Allah.' People are still claiming that he's a Kenyan Muslim.<br /> <br /> Celebrity is a more consistently important element in the presidential race than it was before. Couple that with the always-on internet news cycle, social media, and how fast information travels now and I'd expect campaigns to get louder and more pressured as time goes by. Especially since we can now dig up things people have said or done thirty years ago to keep people talking about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say what you will about the Queen, at least she never called Mexicans rapists and tried to build a wall to keep them out and at least she knows enough to keep private emails private and not to conspire with Guardian &quot;journalists&quot; to smear Bernie Sanders falsely as a mysgonist. </div> </div> </div>They're building a wall to keep out the migrants from Calais, and the royal family did have their voicemail hacked by a British news agency. But yes, the border Britain shares with Mexico is of little concern and I'm sure no one in the royal family cares who Bernie Sanders is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-29-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:47:01-07:00","id":995241,"title":"","content":"Oh its a thing, I've had my chops busted about the Monarchy by Americans, especially when I suggest they get rid of the Presidency as an archiac institution (yeah I know, fair is fair, but the Queen is a good tourist trap when she visits and she doesn't interfer in goverence, require a confusing electoral college).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:41:52-07:00","id":995280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995205#post995205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's only 5-6 points behind Clinton, which is pretty goddamn worrying for us as a nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's worrying from the context of either the presidential election, or even the congressional elections. It's more worrying from the sense of a lack of disruption of the polarization of the country. As much as we can try to compare this election to past elections, in the past you would expect the Republicans to see such massive abandonment of the presidential nominee on the voter level that we'd be talking about if Trump gets any states at all, but the polarization factor is now so strong that he'll get ~200 electoral college votes just for having the R next to his name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Clinton winning is important, but Clinton winning <i>definitively </i>is even more important. It determines how she's viewed by the public and how the RNC and DNC accordingly respond. It determines how much push she has against her policy, and it could have a major effect on how and how quickly the Republican Party crumbles. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not convinced this is the case. I don't think the majority of the Republican party - establishment types or not - have accepted that the last eight years of obstructionism was a bad idea; partially because they're not paying nearly the price for it they would have historically. As long as the Republicans have the House against a Clinton presidency, why should Paul Ryan do anything but what he and Boehner have been doing for all this time? Obstruct to deny the Democrats any feathers in their caps, and waste millions on investigations to harass Clinton from getting anything done via executive powers, and use those investigations as red meat for their base to ensure they get re-elected despite not actually accomplishing anything positive?<br /> <br /> Obama had very solid numbers at his back, and it didn't really do him much good in the face of the modern political landscape. I don't think either the DNC or RNC is going to change based on her degree of victory. Once this election is over, both should be far more worried about what happens in 2018 and 2020 because of the potential impact of the upcoming census regardless of the outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995234#post995234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celebrity is a more consistently important element in the presidential race than it was before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's quite accurate. I'd say the kind of celebrity status that matters has changed. Military based celebrity status was traditionally a huge boon in US politics. Even in modern history military service has been seen as a plus - unless there's a successful attempt to subvert it ala Swift Boat - and specifically avoiding military service was a negative; Clinton had to face a lot of negative criticism as a draft dodger even if it didn't cost him the election in the end. Non-military non-governing public service is also something you traditionally wanted to be famous for if you could.<br /> <br /> Even Reagan faced a lot of early political trouble because his celebrity entertainer status was a negative compared to many of his early opponents' more traditional political pluses. He had to work pretty hard before people started taking him seriously as a politician.<br /> <br /> What we've seen is that &quot;social media&quot; celebrity is now a huge deal. Obama used it really well against Mccain and Romney, and it's pretty much 99% of Trumps approach to the campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995241#post995241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh its a thing, I've had my chops busted about the Monarchy by Americans, especially when I suggest they get rid of the Presidency as an archiac institution (yeah I know, fair is fair, but the Queen is a good tourist trap when she visits and she doesn't interfer in goverence, require a confusing electoral college).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume that has a lot to do with two things.<br /> <br /> First, Americans despise the idea of equating the US Presidency to a monarch. It's an essential part of our cultural political identity that we rejected monarchy and made sure our head of state was a highly constrained position. In the US, calling the sitting President &quot;king&quot; is a step below calling them a traitor. It's meant to be entirely derogatory as a declaration that the President is betraying the ideals of the country. So comparing the presidency to a monarchy is frequently perceived as an insult to our democracy as a whole.<br /> <br /> Second, the US President is not really equivalent to the Queen in position. Getting rid of the President is more like getting rid of the Prime Minister in most countries. Comparing the President to the Queen is betraying a pretty large lack of seriousness in what those positions do in their respective societies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:14:32-07:00","id":995296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995280#post995280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's worrying from the context of either the presidential election, or even the congressional elections. It's more worrying from the sense of a lack of disruption of the polarization of the country. As much as we can try to compare this election to past elections, in the past you would expect the Republicans to see such massive abandonment of the presidential nominee on the voter level that we'd be talking about if Trump gets any states at all, but the polarization factor is now so strong that he'll get ~200 electoral college votes just for having the R next to his name.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm honestly not convinced this is the case. I don't think the majority of the Republican party - establishment types or not - have accepted that the last eight years of obstructionism was a bad idea; partially because they're not paying nearly the price for it they would have historically. As long as the Republicans have the House against a Clinton presidency, why should Paul Ryan do anything but what he and Boehner have been doing for all this time? Obstruct to deny the Democrats any feathers in their caps, and waste millions on investigations to harass Clinton from getting anything done via executive powers, and use those investigations as red meat for their base to ensure they get re-elected despite not actually accomplishing anything positive?<br /> <br /> Obama had very solid numbers at his back, and it didn't really do him much good in the face of the modern political landscape. I don't think either the DNC or RNC is going to change based on her degree of victory. Once this election is over, both should be far more worried about what happens in 2018 and 2020 because of the potential impact of the upcoming census regardless of the outcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's quite accurate. I'd say the kind of celebrity status that matters has changed. Military based celebrity status was traditionally a huge boon in US politics. Even in modern history military service has been seen as a plus - unless there's a successful attempt to subvert it ala Swift Boat - and specifically avoiding military service was a negative; Clinton had to face a lot of negative criticism as a draft dodger even if it didn't cost him the election in the end. Non-military non-governing public service is also something you traditionally wanted to be famous for if you could.<br /> <br /> Even Reagan faced a lot of early political trouble because his celebrity entertainer status was a negative compared to many of his early opponents' more traditional political pluses. He had to work pretty hard before people started taking him seriously as a politician.<br /> <br /> What we've seen is that &amp;quot;social media&amp;quot; celebrity is now a huge deal. Obama used it really well against Mccain and Romney, and it's pretty much 99% of Trumps approach to the campaign.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd assume that has a lot to do with two things.<br /> <br /> First, Americans despise the idea of equating the US Presidency to a monarch. It's an essential part of our cultural political identity that we rejected monarchy and made sure our head of state was a highly constrained position. In the US, calling the sitting President &amp;quot;king&amp;quot; is a step below calling them a traitor. It's meant to be entirely derogatory as a declaration that the President is betraying the ideals of the country. So comparing the presidency to a monarchy is frequently perceived as an insult to our democracy as a whole.<br /> <br /> Second, the US President is not really equivalent to the Queen in position. Getting rid of the President is more like getting rid of the Prime Minister in most countries. Comparing the President to the Queen is betraying a pretty large lack of seriousness in what those positions do in their respective societies.</div> </div> </div> </div> President and Prime Minister are very different positions, a Prime Minister can't govern if he or she doesn't have the confedience of the legislature. Congress and the Senate can both hate the Presidents guts with the legislature and the executive can cripple each others ability to function. The supreme court and state governments is enough of a check and balance to elected power, you don't need a President and Congress and Senate, all fighting each, state governments, and the Supreme Court. Its amazing anything gets done in America, its time to join us in the 21st century and adapt a parliamentary system using mixed member proportional rep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:55:43-07:00","id":995306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995296#post995296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">President and Prime Minister are very different positions, a Prime Minister can't govern if he or she doesn't have the confedience of the legislature.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are different yes, but they're closer to each other than the President is to the Queen.<br /> <br /> And while the US system of checks and balances works differently, the President's ability to govern is largely predicated on having the confidence of the legislature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The supreme court and state governments is enough of a check and balance to elected power, you don't need a President and Congress and Senate, all fighting each, state governments, and the Supreme Court. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Need&quot; is a bit of a loaded word choice, but based on our Constitution those layers are in fact important to ensuring a functional country.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its amazing anything gets done in America, its time to join us in the 21st century and adapt a parliamentary system using mixed member proportional rep. </div> </div> </div>First, it's impossible to just &quot;adapt&quot; an entirely different method of governing. You're talking about completely rewriting the foundational documents of our country.<br /> <br /> Second, you seem to not actually know the variety of parliamentary systems out there. You talk about not needing all these different governing bodies... but the UK system - since it has to grapple with being a union of internally sovereign nations much like the US - has governing bodies below Parliament for the non-England nations within the UK, two houses of Parliament, and so on. Some parliaments allow direct election of the PM instead of the PM being chosen indirectly by the majority party/coalition which creates the same sort of executive/legislative tension you seem to think is unique to the US system. <br /> <br /> Ultimately all democracies, the US system and others, function as well as the people demand of it. The US systems works fine when the people are engaged and put good governance over ideological purity. It grinds to a halt when factionalization and party loyalty are what the people vote for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T04:28:59-07:00","id":995583,"title":"","content":"The days of working past idealogical difference is over and I doubt its coming back.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt, I love America, you guys can be entertaining, but I hate the American political system and think its beyond its best days. I say it because I care and want America to prosper.<br /> <br /> Not saying Canada is perfect, our Senate should be scrapped as the piece of shit that it is and the housecof commons should drop first past the post in favour of mixed member proportional representation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T05:31:57-07:00","id":995590,"title":"","content":"I don't like how people are now going after Trumps kids. Both Trump and Hillary's childern should be left alone, I mean freedom of speech so people have the right, but its sleezy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T06:10:41-07:00","id":995598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995590#post995590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like how people are now going after Trumps kids. Both Trump and Hillary's childern should be left alone, I mean freedom of speech so people have the right, but its sleezy.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about Bill Clinton? How do you feel about his history being brought up in the context of the Clinton campaign?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:36:22-07:00","id":995628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995590#post995590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like how people are now going after Trumps kids. Both Trump and Hillary's childern should be left alone, I mean freedom of speech so people have the right, but its sleezy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That depends, honestly. Barron is still a child, and Tiffany seems to have worked to stay out of the spotlight, so there's no reason for them to be targeted.<br /> <br /> But the rest of Trump's kids are adults who have been involved in his campaign. They've involved themselves publicly with their dad's affairs, and they shouldn't be immune from criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:51:07-07:00","id":995634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995590#post995590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like how people are now going after Trumps kids. Both Trump and Hillary's childern should be left alone, I mean freedom of speech so people have the right, but its sleezy.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, when the kids are out actively engaging in politics, giving speeches and trying to get their parents elected, the media and others should absolutely be allowed to question the things they have done and said. With Trump's younger children who have not had any real presence on the campaign trail, obviously it's in poor form for people to go after them. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I think Bill Clinton is a fine target too as, again, he's gone out on the campaign trail to support his wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:52:07-07:00","id":995728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995583#post995583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The days of working past idealogical difference is over and I doubt its coming back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? People like to talk about how unique and historic this election is, and it is certainly not the average election, but our country has been here in this specific regard before. Eventually things snap back - though it has been devastating in the past in various minor and extreme ways - so they can start growing apart again. I mean, I get why it can seem so horrible, and there's always the chance that this time around the cycle of polarization we finally spin off the rails completely (though the Civil War didn't do us in...), but history suggests we'll muddle through. The question is far more how much damage it ends up doing; and not just this election because this didn't actually start with this election.<br /> <br /> As well, from an American perspective, it always feels weird to have people try to pin this on our oddball system. A lot of countries are struggling with a rise of neo-fascists and populism. Mainstream European style parliament didn't stop the Torries from getting in bed with UKIP. Our way of doing things is different, and thus looks different, but there's a much larger social issue going on in the world than whats' going on here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:30:19-07:00","id":995745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995728#post995728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, from an American perspective, it always feels weird to have people try to pin this on our oddball system. A lot of countries are struggling with a rise of neo-fascists and populism. Mainstream European style parliament didn't stop the Torries from getting in bed with UKIP. Our way of doing things is different, and thus looks different, but there's a much larger social issue going on in the world than whats' going on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certain aspects of America's political system, like the over-the-top gerrymandering and closed primaries that help lead to some of the issues we're facing today. In many parts of the country, the voting numbers are so gerrymandered that you already know which party will win. So the only race that matters is the primary to see what candidate the party puts up.<br /> <br /> In these kind of primaries, being seen as too moderate, too centrist or too willing to work across the aisle is often a death sentence. This leads to more radicals (on the left and right) getting elected (especially to State legislatures but also the House) - radicals who are uninterested in compromise and who, in fact, worry that being seen as too willing to work with their political opponents could cost them their next election.<br /> <br /> But yeah, to a large degree there's a rising tide of anti-immigrant, and nationalistic sentiment throughout most of Europe (look no further than the Brexit), and parts of Asia, so it's not like America is particularly unique in this particular aspect, though I think there are some ways in which America's political system does tend to inflame certain issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:19:18-07:00","id":995774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995745#post995745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This leads to more radicals (on the left and right) getting elected (especially to State legislatures but also the House) - radicals who are uninterested in compromise and who, in fact, worry that being seen as too willing to work with their political opponents could cost them their next election.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHave you paid attention to the Democratic primaries across the United States? Radicals are most certainly not the ones wining those primaries and the claim that both sides are electing radicals is very much a false equivalency. The Democrats are deathly afraid of being painted as radical and work very hard to keep those that buck the status quo out of office, particularly so in Southern states. They are also the party that talks of working across the aisle as a positive, a statement that is a death sentence to any campaign being run by a GOP candidate (as you pointed out). There is a fundamental difference in the beliefs of the two parties' bases about the value in working with the opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:01:23-07:00","id":995797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995774#post995774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHave you paid attention to the Democratic primaries across the United States? Radicals are most certainly not the ones wining those primaries and the claim that both sides are electing radicals is very much a false equivalency. The Democrats are deathly afraid of being painted as radical and work very hard to keep those that buck the status quo out of office, particularly so in Southern states. They are also the party that talks of working across the aisle as a positive, a statement that is a death sentence to any campaign being run by a GOP candidate (as you pointed out). There is a fundamental difference in the beliefs of the two parties' bases about the value in working with the opposition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your right, the democrats don't pick radicals, that takes courage which too far democrats have in short supple and the ones who do have it, don't plan long term and aren't ruthless enough to make the kind of sacrifices need to advance they're agenda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Swu0pil0eeY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Swu0pil0eeY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Swu0pil0eeY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Swu0pil0eeY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hillary is going to destroy social security according to the Young Turks, only a Democrat can get away with this, yet this still support her, because they don't have the brass ones to risk a Trump presidency, in order to free up the democractic ticket for someone better, and to keep her from damaging social security. <br /> <br /> I don't support Trump, but I also didn't support Steven Harper for PM, but I supported the NDP, because I play the long game and I can accept some bad shit happening in the short term, to get to the better place long term. Which actually started to pay dividends till someone slipped Tom Mulcair a valium and a neutred platform in 2015.<br /> <br /> The left isn't ruthless enough for real progressive change, which is why focus keeps shifting to idenitity politics all the time, easier to attack white male nobodies then the people with actual power and wealth.<br /> <br /> So at the end of the day even when it wins the left loses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:05:27-07:00","id":995798,"title":"","content":"I agree that things like Gerrymandering are a problem that can make things worse, but as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11\" data-vbnamecard=\"11\">Darksider</a> pointed out it doesn't always point in the same direction. Heavily gerrymandered districts are extremely sensitive to the local base of whichever party has been set to control that District. I live in somewhat gerrymandered district (though we don't look it compared to our neighbors) that gives Republicans a fairly reliable 70% of the vote (though if you got rid of the few little odd lines on the map, we'd probably only drop to 65%, so like I said not that gerrymandered). But the Tea Party did very poorly here, because while solidly Republican it's also solidly moderate conservative Republicans that want more pragmatism over purity when it comes to general governance. As an example the idea of shutting down the government instead of actually getting a budget passed was seen in an incredibly poor light here.<br /> <br /> There's also weird things local politicians have to balance because we have a decent sized population of smaller Christian sects that are generally conservative, but balk at things that get perceived as being too pushy on other people (when you don't put a nativity scene up outside your own Church/meeting house because that's too ostentatious, a lot of the &quot;War on Christmas&quot; rheotric doesn't work on you), and get hesitant about politicians that are too hawkish because they feel it contradicts their beliefs in Jesus' teachings.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons I was speculating that if the Republicans have significant control for the 2020 census redistricting, there might be a movement within the establishment to not just redistrict against Democrats, but to try to break up/contain the far right a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:18:45-07:00","id":995802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995171#post995171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Statistician, I feel I must inform you that the odds of Trump winning are currently estimated at 9% by <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2016/upshot/presidential-polls-forecast.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2...-forecast.html</a>, which sounds small until you remember it's darned close to one in ten. So in one of eleven possible futures, President Trump is elected next Tuesday.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995196#post995196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And FiveThirtyEight has the odds just under 20%. Any election is going to come with factors we can't predict, and that's especially true in this election (particularly given the abnormally large number of independent and undecided voters less than two weeks from voting day).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware! If you dig into it you'll find most models use an arbitrary chance that all polling information is completely in error. 538 is the most wary in their trust of polling quality this cycle, hedging their bet with a giant factor they've baked into the model itself. If we <a href=\"http://fivethirtyeight.com/features/election-update-why-our-model-is-more-bullish-than-others-on-trump/\" target=\"_blank\">remove that assumption</a> from 538's model, to use the example I'm familiar with, Clinton's chance of winning the election leaps to 99.8%.<br /> <br /> We can compare to the Princeton Election Consortium model run by Sam Wang's team which doesn't put their thumb on the scales. There are no simulations where Trump can win outside of catastrophic errors by pollsters with election results far outside the 95% confidence interval of his model. To quote Sam, <a href=\"https://twitter.com/samwangphd/status/788544053059153924\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It is totally over. If Trump wins more than 240 electoral votes, I will eat a bug.&quot;</a> This is fundamentally the same argument playing out again from the GOP primary process. Sam Wang warned that Donald Trump was a lock for the nomination using a data-driven process of poll aggregation while Nate Silver was <a href=\"http://election.princeton.edu/2016/05/18/nate-silver-puts-his-finger-on-what-happened/\" target=\"_blank\">adding factors</a> to his model under &quot;The Party Decides&quot; trend to insist that Trump would fall to an establishment candidate far past the point where that was plausible. <br /> <br /> So for this assertion that Trump still has a chance to hold true, we need evidence recent US polling has systemic errors across the board. The most notable has been discussion on the oddities of the tracking polls, where the same panel is polled every day instead of obtaining a new sample. I'm guessing Omega's claim about the polls unreliably is based on the famous LAT tracker story in the NYT about <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/13/upshot/how-one-19-year-old-illinois-man-is-distorting-national-polling-averages.html\" target=\"_blank\">on how one young black man in Illinois</a> who is REALLY excited for Trump has distorted their poll all year. But the tracking polls have favored Trump, so errors there don't help him. Worse, we now have early voting data we could search for evidence that the polls were wrong about a battleground states Trump needs for a path to 270. Republicans normally perform well in early voting only to face a Democratic surge on election day, but their weak ground game is crippling them already in states like Nevada. They were already behind by <a href=\"http://www.ktnv.com/news/ralston/the-nevada-early-voting-blog\" target=\"_blank\">44,000 votes in Clark county</a> this morning when their plan to ferry a Trump rally's worth of potential voters to the polls hit a snag; the promised buses became a paltry <a href=\"https://twitter.com/meganmesserly\" target=\"_blank\">group of vans</a> instead after a several hour wait.<br /> <br /> If you still don't believe me, try to build an electoral path for Donald Trump that gains more than 270+ EVs that makes sense with <a href=\"http://www.electproject.org/early_2016\" target=\"_blank\">early voting data</a> for each battleground state he supposedly will flip. If Trump has a plausible winning map, it shouldn't be hard to create one with a compelling argument behind it... but I've yet to see one that doesn't rely on Nevada, Pennsylvania, Virginia and North Carolina, none of which he can win any longer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:36:16-07:00","id":995808,"title":"","content":"To add to what I was saying compare the Tea Party/Trumpites and Occupy Wall Street.<br /> <br /> 1 year and Occupy Wall street folded like a lawn chair and rightwing business mags were openly bragging about the victory. <br /> <br /> The Tea Party and Trumpites are willing to burn the fucking GOP around their ears, they're as stubborn as a two headed mule. <br /> <br /> Even if Trump loses here, its NOT over, nothing is resolved, its delayed at best.<br /> <br /> My prediction if Donald Trump loses in this year, in 2020 Hillary will be facing Ivanka Trump, and lose. This could be why so many Democracts are starting smear Ivanka in so many ways, from mocking Ivanka's business dealings, to hinting at an incestous relationship with her father, because they know Hillary can't beat Ivanka, who is smarter, younger, more attraction, more well liked, then her father and a woman. With the right platform and right advisers (get rid of the trash largely surrounded Trump, but keep Scott Baio), maybe shift to the left on key issues, show some diplomancy towards latinos, and then proceed to crush Hillary.<br /> <br /> So that is my prediction, this fight is just round 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:41:37-07:00","id":995809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995797#post995797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The left isn't ruthless enough for real progressive change, which is <b>why focus keeps shifting to idenitity politics</b> all the time, easier to attack white male nobodies then the people with actual power and wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting real fucking tired of people like you acting like genuine social progress is some kind of frippery the left is distracting itself with instead of doing real work. 'Identity politics' will stop being important the day that the bigots on the right stop trying to treat their unashamed hate as a valid political stance and enforcing it with discriminatory legislation. <br /> <br /> Nothing has condemned Trump more in my eyes than his choice of Pence as a running mate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:47:02-07:00","id":995811,"title":"","content":"I think Ivanka Trump would have a hard time selling herself to the Christian Republicans with her conversion to Judaism. They could probably see past her not seeing herself as a Republican though. And it would be the height of irony for a Jewish woman from New York to be the face of the Republican Party.<br /> <br /> The GOP has had a weirdly bad streak of candidates in the past few years, I figure it's due to things people have mentioned previously. McCain was probably the strongest, I was on the fence about voting for him, but pairing him up with Sarah Palin to, I can only imagine, help get the women vote was a ridiculous idea. Then Mitt Romney in the middle of the Occupy Wallstreet movement. And more recently people like Ted Cruz, Ben Carson and Donald Trump. They just seem so out of touch. I wouldn't expect any grandly thought out scheme so much as opportunism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_lin