the party of progressives, the party of Lincon, what happens to them anyways?<br /> <br /> Look I was just venting in disgust at what was being done at Ivanka and possibly to a lesser extent his other childern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:08:53-07:00","id":995873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995856#post995856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That disgusting, rude, and ignorant. But they're not trying to Bankurpt her and destroy her, like they are to Ivanka. Its a whole other scale.<br /> <br /> But if they continue I think some republicans will do more then just insult Chelsea, this door should never have been opened, the people behind Ivanka's boycott didn't think about the consquences of their actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are boycotting her line because she's been adamantly supporting her father's hateful ideology, and they see her label being tied up in a fortune that's synonymous with fiscal corruption. Seems perfectly legitimate to me. They're voting with their dollar out of conscientious objection to the values she represents. Why should women want to buy clothing from a woman who defends the misogyny and rape apologism of her father?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T20:37:11-07:00","id":995937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995797#post995797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your right, the democrats don't pick radicals, that takes courage which too far democrats have in short supple and the ones who do have it, don't plan long term and aren't ruthless enough to make the kind of sacrifices need to advance they're agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou mean the kind of courage that got us Governors Brownback and Walker, along with Congressman Louie Gohmert? Thanks, I'd prefer Democrats didn't elect radicals like that, radicals with bad fiscal policy ideas and worse governing ability. It's also an amusing statement to read considering one of the biggest criticisms about Clinton from Trump is that she's a ruthless career politician while he gins up fear in his followers of her getting her &quot;progressive&quot; agenda forced through.<br /> <br /> I'm not interested in playing a game where my team has to win by whatever it takes, because governing the most politically and economically powerful country in the world isn't a fucking game. I'm also not interested in seeing people elected whose party claim is that big government doesn't work and then when in power do everything they can to make government as ineffective as possible.<br /> <br /> I want leaders who don't deny problems exist, don't try to cast blame while denying their part in the creation of said problems, and who are willing to work with their opposition for the greater good of the country rather than their donors interests (while paying lip service to their electorate).<br /> <br /> At this point I'd be happy if the GOP tried something other than trickle down economics instead of touting a solution that has repeatedly failed. I'd like a GOP that doesn't use fearmongering tactics to justify their nativist immigration stances. I'd like a GOP that isn't run by religious fundamentalists, I greatly preferred them when they were the party of business and could compromise on civil rights issues, something they no longer do because the base they cultivated won't allow them to do so. I'd also like a GOP that doesn't cast the poor as the cause of the country's fiscal problems while I'm at it, because nothing screams courage like blaming the most powerless segment of your country for the problems your economic policies created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 10-31-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T06:10:30-07:00","id":996046,"title":"","content":"So, I am going to try to get away from work and early vote today. I figured voting on Halloween is appropriate considering how horrific this election season has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:11:39-07:00","id":996057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=995873#post995873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People are boycotting her line because she's been adamantly supporting her father's hateful ideology, and they see her label being tied up in a fortune that's synonymous with fiscal corruption. Seems perfectly legitimate to me. They're voting with their dollar out of conscientious objection to the values she represents. Why should women want to buy clothing from a woman who defends the misogyny and rape apologism of her father?</div> </div> </div> </div> I see, so its open season on politicians families then, it can be just that she loves her father, not his idealogy or something, and wants to support someone she loves.<br /> <br /> Again, you still don't see how this could blow up in someones face or how going after a politicians family is out of line. You did prove me wrong about one thing, Democracts are radicals, just about all the wrong things.<br /> <br /> Your plenty radical on ruining a woman's life because of the sins of her father, but when it comes to standing up to a corrupt DNC, when it comes to standing up for single payer univeral healthcare system, that could save countless lives, men, women, childern, ect..., your too busy making excuses, and bitching about manspreading, and useless unproductive boycotts of Ivanka Trump, knowing that she can't retailate against you, but sypathizers might got after Chelsea Clinton with a boycott, but hey that's still not you.<br /> <br /> The Democratic Party of America, why think big, when you can think petty!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:11:14-07:00","id":996077,"title":"","content":"You're mistaking private citizens for the Democratic Party.<br /> <br /> One doesn't have to be a member to dislike Trump, things he says, or things his daughter does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:59:34-07:00","id":996102,"title":"","content":"No...? Let's talk about this some more? Because it sounds like you're making some pretty large assumptions about me and how I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996057#post996057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see, so its open season on politicians families then, it can be just that she loves her father, not his idealogy or something, and wants to support someone she loves.</div> </div> </div> </div>She has every right to love her father. She has every right to defend him in private, to support him in private, and to publicly state that she stands behind him. For that matter, she has the right to say abhorrent things in public if she so chooses. But we can't expect for public actions to not influence a person's reputation.<br /> <br /> Ms. Trump's clothing line is a lifestyle brand. It's a brand that sells itself on the Trump name, on Ivanka's name, and on her proposed mission statements for that brand. If you go to her website, the entire focal point, from the soft pastel coloring to the mission statements and write copy, presents itself as feminist first and foremost. It also presents her active involvement in her father's political and corporate interests as qualifications. This isn't about people attacking a civilian family member because she's a member of the opposition party (I would proudly defend attacks against Tiffany, Barron, or any other family member that the press or public tries to turn into a casualty). This is about understandable backlash against a business woman who's consciously built an identity brand and then publicly spoken in terms that contradict that brand. She's a public surrogate for Trump and aggressively involved in his campaign, and she's come out praising him as a feminist and downplaying his aggressively anti-feminist rhetoric and actions. It's ludicrous to think that there wouldn't be a backlash, and I'm comfortable in the knowledge that she's actively made this bed for herself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996057#post996057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you still don't see how this could blow up in someones face or how going after a politicians family is out of line. You did prove me wrong about one thing, Democracts are radicals, just about all the wrong things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going after someone's family for being a member of their family is out of line. Going after someone's family because of the actions that they individually have taken (as Ivanka has) is a whole new ball game. And don't presume I'm a Democrat. I'm not. I'm an actual radical, but that doesn't mean I don't have principles.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest. Trump is never a brand I would have bought into, so the boycott doesn't really affect me one bit. But if American Spirits (who promote themselves as an environmentally friendly company) endorsed the Dakota Pipeline, I'd be quick to reconsider my support about them. Same thing here. Ivanka made the decision to mix politics and business and to do so in contradictory ways. She's not a bystander, and her choices are her own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996057#post996057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your plenty radical on ruining a woman's life because of the sins of her father, but when it comes to standing up to a corrupt DNC, when it comes to standing up for single payer univeral healthcare system, that could save countless lives, men, women, childern, ect..., your too busy making excuses, and bitching about manspreading, and useless unproductive boycotts of Ivanka Trump, knowing that she can't retailate against you, but sypathizers might got after Chelsea Clinton with a boycott, but hey that's still not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it's not about the sins of her father. It's about her own missteps and hypocrisies. I support universal healthcare too. I advocate and vote for candidates that more accurately reflect my views on a regular basis. I also have plenty to dislike about Clinton, but I can vote pragmatically when I need to. Public actions effect brand identity, especially when that's the model around which you've promoted your brand.<br /> <br /> And hey, if Chelsea Clinton starts a principle-focused business and then openly contradicts the values that she sells her product on, a boycott is a perfectly reasonable response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996057#post996057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Democratic Party of America, why think big, when you can think petty!</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern armchair punditry, why think or listen when you can lecture and attack!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-31-2016, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:40:52-07:00","id":996140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996102#post996102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No...? Let's talk about this some more? Because it sounds like you're making some pretty large assumptions about me and how I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> She has every right to love her father. She has every right to defend him in private, to support him in private, and to publicly state that she stands behind him. For that matter, she has the right to say abhorrent things in public if she so chooses. But we can't expect for public actions to not influence a person's reputation.<br /> <br /> Ms. Trump's clothing line is a lifestyle brand. It's a brand that sells itself on the Trump name, on Ivanka's name, and on her proposed mission statements for that brand. If you go to her website, the entire focal point, from the soft pastel coloring to the mission statements and write copy, presents itself as feminist first and foremost. It also presents her active involvement in her father's political and corporate interests as qualifications. This isn't about people attacking a civilian family member because she's a member of the opposition party (I would proudly defend attacks against Tiffany, Barron, or any other family member that the press or public tries to turn into a casualty). This is about understandable backlash against a business woman who's consciously built an identity brand and then publicly spoken in terms that contradict that brand. She's a public surrogate for Trump and aggressively involved in his campaign, and she's come out praising him as a feminist and downplaying his aggressively anti-feminist rhetoric and actions. It's ludicrous to think that there wouldn't be a backlash, and I'm comfortable in the knowledge that she's actively made this bed for herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Going after someone's family for being a member of their family is out of line. Going after someone's family because of the actions that they individually have taken (as Ivanka has) is a whole new ball game. And don't presume I'm a Democrat. I'm not. I'm an actual radical, but that doesn't mean I don't have principles.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest. Trump is never a brand I would have bought into, so the boycott doesn't really affect me one bit. But if American Spirits (who promote themselves as an environmentally friendly company) endorsed the Dakota Pipeline, I'd be quick to reconsider my support about them. Same thing here. Ivanka made the decision to mix politics and business and to do so in contradictory ways. She's not a bystander, and her choices are her own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, it's not about the sins of her father. It's about her own missteps and hypocrisies. I support universal healthcare too. I advocate and vote for candidates that more accurately reflect my views on a regular basis. I also have plenty to dislike about Clinton, but I can vote pragmatically when I need to. Public actions effect brand identity, especially when that's the model around which you've promoted your brand.<br /> <br /> And hey, if Chelsea Clinton starts a principle-focused business and then openly contradicts the values that she sells her product on, a boycott is a perfectly reasonable response.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Modern armchair punditry, why think or listen when you can lecture and attack!</div> </div> </div> </div> You rationalize all you like, when the results are President Ivanka in 2020, I don't to hear your tears, because YOU MADE YOUR BED in 2016.<br /> <br /> Ivanka was more interested in building in her business, I doubt she would have run in 2020, but if this shit keep up, yep she'll be coming in 2020 for revenge and she will win. <br /> <br /> You rationalize all you want, you reap what you sow.<br /> <br /> (Caveat, you have freedom of speech, when I say I don't want to hear...I mean I'll roll my eyes, say I warned you, and then ignore your complaints).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:55:08-07:00","id":996147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=996140#post996140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You rationalize all you like, when the results are President Ivanka in 2020, I don't to hear your tears, because YOU MADE YOUR BED in 2016.<br /> <br /> Ivanka was more interested in building in her business, I doubt she would have run in 2020, but if this shit keep up, yep she'll be coming in 2020 for revenge and she will win.<br /> <br /> You rationalize all you want, you reap what you sow.<br /> <br /> (Caveat, you have freedom of speech, when I say I don't want to hear...I mean I'll roll my eyes, say I warned you, and then ignore your complaints).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rationalize all I want, but you'll ignore my rationale?<br /> <br /> Got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name